"""Carnival ports of call: canonical names from the upstream cruise-search API
schedules; day-tile descriptions and images from upstream itinerary pages
(scraped_data/itins/*.json, 2026-09-22)."""

# 174 ports (173 with upstream descriptions)
PORTS = [
    {'code': 'A50', 'name': 'Ship Meetups', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'ship-meetups', 'desc_html': "The unique ship meetup means that your cruise is bigger than just a cruise. Your ship will be throwing its own party, but the other ships in the area will be too, so meeting up and hanging out nearby makes our celebration even bigger. This neat trick is one we only pull out when it's time to mark a major milestone!", 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-itinerary-ship-meetups-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ACA', 'name': 'Acapulco', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'acapulco', 'desc_html': "Located way down Mexico's Pacific Coast, Acapulco is famous as an exotic destination that became something of a legendary resort hotspot for mid-century celebrities. Visitors of today are rewarded with more than just the iconic beaches they all come expecting — which are spectacular, don't get us wrong — this is a place where culture and nature make up equal parts of the Acapulco story. Don't miss the famous cliff divers, not to mention the dramatic cliffs, of La Quebrada. The Fort of San Diego, dating back to the 1600s, is now a museum of archaeology, Mexican independence, and even piracy. And, of course, you can't visit and not stroll the Malecón!", 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-panama-canal-itinerary-acapulco-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'AGP', 'name': 'Málaga', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'malaga', 'desc_html': 'Cruise to M&aacute;laga and enjoy one of Spain&rsquo;s oldest cities. First founded by the Phoenicians, the city of M&aacute;laga had hosted a number of civilizations over its 3,000 years. The end result is a city that&rsquo;s a cornucopia of Roman and Moorish influences, among others. Travel to M&aacute;laga and enjoy the city&rsquo;s many museums, especially Museo Picasso M&aacute;laga&hellip; after all, this is the city where the artist himself was born. Take a side-trip to nearby Granada, where visitors can explore the Alhambra, a UNESCO World Heritage Site that&rsquo;s at once an imposing fortress, impressive palace and a small town.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Discover one of Spain&rsquo;s greatest traditions at its largest and oldest bullfighting arena.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the Alhambra and explore this 14th century palace.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take a guided tour of the M&aacute;laga Cathedral with its unique mix of styles. </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-port-malaga-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'AJA', 'name': 'Ajaccio, Corsica', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'ajaccio-corsica', 'desc_html': 'Ajaccio has a historical fact to get out of the way before we proceed, and it’s not a small one. This is the town where Napoleon was born… you know, the legendary French emperor? Visit the city, the capital of the island of Corsica, and walk in his footsteps as you explore what they call “The Scented Isle.” If you’re wondering why they would do that, you only need to get a bit outside of the city and find <em>le maquis</em>, an aromatic bush that’s native to the island and easy to spot thanks to its cool shade of purple. But there’s plenty to see in back in local civilization, like the Roman Catholic Cathedral from the 16th Century, Maison Bonaparte (Napoleon’s birthplace) and an amazing collection of art at the Fesch Museum.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-port-ajaccio-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ALC', 'name': 'Alicante', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'alicante', 'desc_html': '<p>A beach resort town on the Mediterranean coast — that’s an instant “ahhh” from you, right? Alicante is just that kind of place, with options for getting you in touch with some white sand, chilling in the shade of palm trees or exploring old-world charm. The city’s own “old town” section is as good for strolling as it is shopping, while some of the best views are conveniently available at Castillo de Santa Barbara fortress, which visitors access through an underground tunnel. Spanish-style dining should be on your to-do list, so come hungry and set aside some time for a leisurely multi-course lunch, a meal at a seafront café or a visit to an Ayuntamiento neighborhood tapas bar. Nourishment for the soul is served up at Museo de Arte Siglo, which houses works by Dali, Miro and Picasso. While Alicante was founded by the Romans as <em>Lucentum</em>, even visitors of today will see why “city of lights” is still a fitting description for this vibrant Spanish spot.</p>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-port-alicante-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'AMS', 'name': 'Amsterdam', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'amsterdam', 'desc_html': 'Amsterdam was the world’s most prosperous city in the 17th century, a time when Dutch power was at its peak. While things have changed, many of the city’s Golden Age treasures are well-preserved for visitors of today! One is the city’s elaborate system of canals, which continues to capture the imagination — and feature in the photography — of visitors. On dry land folks will find some of the finest art museums anywhere, including both the Van Gogh and the Rijksmuseum. Amsterdamers love to get around by bike and the city boasts nearly 250 miles (around 400 km) of bike paths. This family-friendly city has a flavor about it, and you’ll always find something to your taste, whether it’s a casual bite of hot, fresh stroopwafel or a laid-back visit to a <em>bruine kroeg</em> (brown café), a unique breed of establishment known as much for their hospitality and character as their food.<ul class="features-list">\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See how things go ‘round at Zaanse Schans, home of iconic and colorful windmills.</li>\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour The Hague — The Netherlands’ administrative center and home of the king and queen.</li>\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Marvel at what’s in bloom at Keukenhof, featuring 80 acres of flowering tulips, daffodils and more.</li>\r\n  </ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-amsterdam-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'AOJ', 'name': 'Aomori', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'aomori', 'desc_html': 'Today, many of the best sights to see in Aomori are the natural kind, as much of the man-made history was lost to various 20<sup style="font-size:12px; line-height:12px;">th</sup> Century misfortunes. Yet no one seems to have told the cherry blossoms, apple orchards and the mountainous backdrop, all of which greet visitors with a timeless serenity. The region’s two national parks and highly aesthetic Lake Towada are similarly still just doing their thing. In the city, in case you miss Aomori’s annual Nebuta Matsuri Festival, the Nebuta Warasse Museum will let you feast your eyes on some of the incredible illuminated floats that graced the streets. And just outside the city at Seiryu-ji Temple, all 70 feet and 220 tons of Showa Daibutsu statue (“the Great Buddha”) keeps a watchful eye over Aomori.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/AU/Aomori-Temple-Bridge-Autumn-Garden-v1-1920x1080-jpg.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ARB', 'name': 'Aruba', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'aruba', 'desc_html': 'It&rsquo;s hard to find a more beautiful vacation destination than the Southern Caribbean, and on our cruises to Aruba, you&rsquo;re the star of that perfect snapshot. Splash and play your way across this sparkling corner of the Caribbean, or simply relax on a sun-baked beach on one of Carnival&rsquo;s cruises to Aruba. The locals call it the &ldquo;happy island,&rdquo; and they prove it &mdash; Aruba cheerily welcomes visitors to picture-perfect strips of beach, swaths of exotic blooms, and some of the Caribbean&rsquo;s top shopping and nightlife locales. Celebrate the year-round Caribbean spirit, or simply unwind to the island&rsquo;s bewitching and relaxing tempo. It&rsquo;s easy to find your own tropical beat when you cruise Aruba-style.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Lounge on the white sands of world-class Palm Beach.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Hop aboard the famous Kukoo Kunuku bus for a fun-filled island tour, and then relax on Mambo beach.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See why visitors can&rsquo;t wait to get down to snorkeling and scuba.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop for fine Dutch-made porcelain and imported chocolates in Oranjestad.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-aruba-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ARH', 'name': 'Aarhus', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'aarhus', 'desc_html': 'Aarhus is the second-largest city in Denmark and it isn’t even close — the capital Copenhagen has well over double the population. But this somewhat smaller city has a charm and laid-back vibe that more than makes up for it. A surprising amount of the city still has its traditional Danish buildings, and there’s even been architectural discoveries that now date its founding back to the year 770. But just as much around here is modern and vibrant, including a culture of fine dining where chefs regularly pick up top international awards, and the street food scene is just as delicious. Outside of the built world, the city is surrounded by forests… and Denmark’s nearby Lake District isn’t just iconic, but it’s actually where the queen of Denmark has her summer home.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-aarhus-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ATG', 'name': 'Antigua', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'antigua', 'desc_html': 'Discover your own slice of paradise &mdash; the white-sand kind &mdash; when you sail on cruises to Antigua. Here, legend has it, there&rsquo;s actually a beach for every day of the year. (Leap years will have to share a little.) When you cruise to Antigua, located right in the heart of the Caribbean, you can&rsquo;t help but notice relics of the island&rsquo;s British colonial past &mdash; high tea is an afternoon ritual and cricket is the local passion, but this independent nation&rsquo;s sunny island vibe reigns supreme. Cruises to Antigua are a great way to immerse yourself in all of it &mdash; the charming English culture and the irresistible Caribbean sunshine. Best of all? A Carnival cruise to Antigua makes it all a breeze. Got all that, chap?<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Swim in the clear, warm seas off one of the island&rsquo;s 365 beaches.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy the opportunity to swim with majestic stingrays at Antigua\'s famed Stingray Village.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take a tour of historic English Harbour and Nelson&rsquo;s Dockyard National Park.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Marvel at the Antigua rainforest by taking a canopy tour.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-antigua-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ATH', 'name': 'Piraeus (Athens)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'piraeus-athens', 'desc_html': 'Cruise to Athens, Greece and fall in love with the city&rsquo;s unique claims to fame. This one-of-a-kind, history-rich destination can  boast to not only be the home to the Olympic games throughout the ages&hellip; but also the birthplace of democracy. Talk about competitive team sports! To this day, Athens is a city as rich in history as it is immersed in mythology. On cruises from Athens, you&rsquo;ll see ancient feats of architecture like the Acropolis, Parthenon and Temple of Olympian Zeus mingling with modern museums, cafes and shops across the Athenian landscape. It&rsquo;s a one-of-a-kind destination, and a must-see stop on any Greek Isles cruise.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the Parthenon and you&rsquo;re in Athena&rsquo;s house. This temple, built to worship her, today welcomes all.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Get it together and visit the Temple of Hephaestus &mdash; perhaps the best-preserved ancient temple.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Pl&aacute;ka, a neighborhood located just a stone&rsquo;s throw from major historical sites, is an historical destination, itself.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-athens-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BAR', 'name': 'Bar', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'bar', 'desc_html': 'If you were the third-largest city in Montenegro, that doesn\'t actually make you a big city — which is why Bar can sit comfortably high in the rankings but still have that personal touch. You won\'t be surprised to find out that it\'s considered something of a resort town, but you\'ll be pleased to hear that its location makes it a great place for exploring Montenegro\'s Adriatic coastal region, including its beaches, nature and culture. Local history is on display at the town\'s "old town," the hilltop Stari Bar area, which was first settled by the Romans in the 6th century, and much of Bar\'s coastline is charming pebble-lined beach. But beyond the town is more regional goodness for travelers to discover, like the preserved Medieval city of Kotor that\'s set on a fjord, and the town of Budva, whose history dates back to the B.C. times and can claim to be older than just about anything else on the Adriatic coast.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-bar-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BCN', 'name': 'Barcelona', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'barcelona', 'desc_html': 'Cruises from Barcelona make for some of the most unforgettable vacations you can imagine. Barcelona looks like a city that should be known for its architecture&hellip; and, naturally, it is. From monuments in Romanesque and Renaissance styles to Gothic spires and contemporary curves, there&rsquo;s little surprise Barcelona was the creative playground of acclaimed architect Antoni Gaud&iacute;. But that&rsquo;s just one reason why cruises out of Barcelona are so seductive. Barcelona&rsquo;s a feast for the eyes and the palate, alike, and be sure not to miss the chance to try tapas as and visit spots like the La Rambla, Port Vell and especially Gaud&iacute;&rsquo;s Sagrada Familia Cathedral. Fun beach bars overlooking the Mediterranean, sleek Spanish designer stores, and Gaud&iacute;&rsquo;s surreal buildings make Barcelona, Spain a whimsical and unique place to visit. For a Mediterranean cruise, Spain is a great place to start &mdash; sample the good stuff on one of Carnival&rsquo;s cruises from Barcelona.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Cruise to Barcelona to photograph Gaud&iacute;&rsquo;s otherworldly sculptures in Park G&uuml;ell.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Ascend Montju&iuml;c Hill for stunning city views.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enter the 14th-century Catedral&rsquo;s vaulted galleries and listen for its 13 resident geese.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-barcelona-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BDS', 'name': 'Barbados', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'barbados', 'desc_html': 'Barbados cruises give you the chance to experience tropical life with a refined twist. With pearly pink sand and a jaunty British lilt, Barbados is one of the Caribbean&rsquo;s most captivating islands. Whether you&rsquo;re cruising to or from Barbados, discover a hothouse landscape where old sugar plantations and rum distilleries dot the verdant sun-dappled hills. Or, start your travels here and give yourself more time to get immersed in the local culture while you vacation in Barbados. Spy a green monkey in a rainforest ravine, sample savory local rum, or simply follow the trail of bougainvillea blossoms to a glorious beach with Carnival cruises to Barbados.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Lounge on luscious pink- and white-sand beaches.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore the sparkling crystals and underground pools in Harrison&rsquo;s Cave.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy a tour and a tipple at the Mount Gay Rum Distillery<sup style="font-size: 70%;">&reg;</sup>.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-barbados-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BEO', 'name': 'Benoa (Denpasar)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'benoa-denpasar', 'desc_html': 'There’s a reason so many people love Bali cruises, and it’s easy to see why. Enjoy the white sand beaches, visit sacred temples, experience active volcanoes and ancient rice paddies and soak in everything Benoa (Bali) has to offer. And make the most of our Bali cruises with more than 45 onboard activities, with a lot of fun and adventure for people of all ages. Incense, frangipani, and the distant echo of gamelan announce Bali before you\'ve even stepped off the tender. Whether you\'re drawn to spiritual ceremonies in Ubud, the temple gates at Tanah Lot, or the colour of Seminyak\'s beach clubs, a single port day puts it all within reach. <br /><br />\n\nFrom Benoa, your Bali options are genuinely extraordinary. Drive north to Ubud for the famous Tegallalang Rice Terraces and a stop at the Sacred Monkey Forest. Head west along the coast for sunset at Tanah Lot, perched on its sea rock as the tide rolls in. For something more active, surf lessons at Kuta Beach, white-water rafting on the Ayung River and cycling through village lanes all make for excellent cruise-day excursions. Food lovers should make for Seminyak\'s café strip or a local warung for nasi goreng, satay lilit and black rice pudding with fresh coconut milk. A Bali cruise may be a single day at sea, but it\'s a day Bali makes every minute count. <br /><br />\n\nA Carnival cruise to Bali is the easiest way to experience the island without the planning fatigue. Come as you are, step ashore into one of the world\'s most captivating destinations and let Bali do the rest. Browse our latest cruises to Bali and Indonesia and book with Carnival today.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li>\n    <em class="dest-check"></em>\n    Active volcanoes and sacred temples.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n    <em class="dest-check"></em>\n    White sand beaches of Nusa Dua.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n    <em class="dest-check"></em>\n    White water rafting everyone will love.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n    <em class="dest-check"></em>\n    Sacred temples and natural beauty.\n    </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/CCLAU/cruise-to/bali-hero-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BFT', 'name': 'Belfast', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'belfast', 'desc_html': 'Discover Northern Ireland&rsquo;s rejuvenated capital on your European cruise to Belfast. A beacon of triumph and resilience, Belfast is a thriving city where Victorian splendor mixes with 21<sup>st</sup> century museums, revitalized docklands, and a buzzing dining scene. The birthplace of the RMS Titanic, Belfast is home to one of the world&rsquo;s largest exhibits on the subject, which is currently housed on the site of the shipyard where the famed vessel was actually built. Make time to explore the countryside on your Belfast cruise and experience the extraordinary landscape unique to Northern Ireland.<ul class="features-list">\n\t<li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tBehold the stunning natural beauty of the Glens of Antrim.\n\t</li>\n    <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tVisit the birthplace of the Titanic to discover its secrets, history, and legacy.\n\t</li>\n    <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tWalk the ancient seafront rock formations of the Giant&rsquo;s Causeway.\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tGaze at intricate mosaic ceilings at St. Anne\'s Cathedral.\n\t</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-belfast-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BIM', 'name': 'Bimini', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'bimini', 'desc_html': 'Are there words more fun to say than “I’m cruising to Bimini!”? The name rolls off the tongue delightfully, for sure… but the whole phrase means you’re in for a beautiful, uniquely chill time in this island chain. The center of the action is Alice Town, though “action” is relative when it comes to these westernmost islands of The Bahamas. The local aesthetics, however, will take your breath away — and fishing, diving and relaxing on a beach are a few of the choice activities for experiencing the naturally azure waters surrounding Bimini, which are great enjoyed from a distance or up-close!', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-bahamas-itinerary-bimini-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BIO', 'name': 'Bilbao', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'bilbao', 'desc_html': 'Bilbao is set a ways away from Spain’s best-known destinations like Madrid and Barcelona, but there are reasons to seek out a cruise to the largest city in Basque Country. BC’s an “autonomous community” that Spain considers its own nation and comes complete with its own language. Your ship’s approach to the city is Ria del Bilbao and this waterway affords you your first look at the surrounding mountains that — get used to it! — are going to be featuring prominently in your photos. Tourism is huge here, and it’s a great sign that so many of Bilbao’s visitors come from other parts of Spain. What attracts them? It might be the city’s collection of museums, including the famous one with the crazy-cool exterior and all the modern art inside. But it could very well be the food. Basque cuisine is world-class with award-winning chefs all over the place… so, no joke, if you spend most of your visit on fine dining nobody would bat an eye.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the ancient Basque capital of Guernica, a name made infamous by Picasso’s 1930s painting.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Walk Bilbao’s cobblestone streets and cross the city’s 17 bridges.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore the seaside resort town of San Sebastian, a Basque Country highlight that practically straddles Spain’s border with France. </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-bilbao-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BNE', 'name': 'Brisbane', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'brisbane', 'desc_html': '<p>Whether you’re departing or arriving in Brisbane, you’ll be surrounded by an offering of adventure and endless amounts of fun. Think sunshine, relaxation and a holiday the whole family will love! </p>\n<ul class="features-list">\n\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Enjoy picture-perfect cruise holidays.\n    </li>\n \n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Indulge in more than 45 onboard activities.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Create memories with cruises from Brisbane.\n    </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/CCLAU/cruise-from/brisbane-hero-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BON', 'name': 'Bonaire', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'bonaire', 'desc_html': 'Bonaire is an island nation in the Southern Caribbean that was twice &ldquo;discovered&rdquo; &mdash; once by the Spanish and once by the Dutch &mdash; and was until recently part of the Netherlands Antilles. Its far-flung history may be all over the map&hellip; but you&rsquo;ll find the island itself located just right. Also just right is the climate &mdash; the annual average is 81.5&deg; F &mdash; so you&rsquo;ll have plenty of reasons to spend time outdoors. When in the water, diving and snorkeling happen to be some of the best ways to see the reef surrounding the island&hellip; but they&rsquo;re also great for cooling off.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy world-class snorkeling in crystal-clear water among coral reefs that line the coasts of Bonaire.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour Lac Bay National Park aboard a powerboat &mdash; the park is one of the best-preserved mangrove forests in the Caribbean.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See the salt beds in Pekelmeer, also home to thousands of pink flamingoes.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-bonaire-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BRI', 'name': 'Bari', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'bari', 'desc_html': 'Tucked along the sparkling Adriatic in Italy’s Puglia region, Bari remains a delightful secret waiting to be discovered. Few travelers venture to this vibrant port city, yet those who do are rewarded with layers of history, culture, and unforgettable food woven into everyday life. Wander through Old Town’s winding streets, where you can watch locals make fresh pasta by hand, pop into centuries-old churches, and soak up the energy of lively piazzas. Stroll through a cinematic historic center, admire medieval castles and grand cathedrals, or explore the surrounding coastline, where cliffs and crystal-clear waters set the scene. From bustling markets to local trattorias serving fresh, regional specialties, Bari offers authentic southern Italian charm for the curious and adventurous alike.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-bari-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BUE', 'name': 'Buenos Aires', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'buenos-aires', 'desc_html': 'If you mixed "old world charm" and "new world swagger," it would probably taste a little like dulce de leche... a beloved treat that Argentina is famous for inventing! Delicious as it is, food is just one of Argentina\'s claims to fame, and the local attractions and architecture keep up with the flavors just fine. Tango is another top export best enjoyed direct from the source, and the energetic Palermo Viejo nightlife is practically palpable during the day. This world city has been compared to Paris, and the history, old-fashioned confitería\xa0cafés and colonial architecture certainly all play their role, and despite all the modernity, plenty of green spaces remain. But if you\'re looking for the rest of the colors of the rainbow, the buildings of the riverside La Boca neighborhood show them off to visitors in all their vibrant splendor.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-south-america-itinerary-buenos-aires-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BWI', 'name': 'Baltimore', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'baltimore', 'desc_html': '<p>Set sail from the Charm City&rsquo;s historic harbor on Carnival cruises from Baltimore, Maryland. Many of Baltimore&rsquo;s vibrant neighborhoods and most important sights &mdash; including the original Star-Spangled Banner waving over Fort McHenry &mdash; can be found near the lively seaport, making it a snap to get a taste of the city. A collection of museums, markets, and maritime activities &mdash; like a thriving centuries-old marketplace &mdash; will start your Carnival cruise from Baltimore in style.&nbsp;Then, once you&rsquo;re aboard, your ship will open the door to a host of new adventures. With destinations like Bermuda, The Bahamas and the Caribbean, cruises out of Baltimore have the variety to please everyone in your party.</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll among the buzzing shops and maritime sites of the Inner Harbor.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Cheer for the hometown Baltimore Orioles during the summer baseball season.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Catch an artillery demonstration at the Revolutionary War-era Fort McHenry.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Snack on sweet treats at an old-world cafe in Little Italy.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-baltimore-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'BZE', 'name': 'Belize', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'belize', 'desc_html': 'There are plenty of reasons why a cruise to Belize should top your travel bucket list. A tropical paradise that promises adventure, both onshore and off? You better Belize it! Crystalline rivers flow through impressive lowland jungles, home to wildlife of various stripes. (And various spots.) Silky-sand beaches, waving palms and colorful coral gardens are just part of Belize&rsquo;s natural wonders. And they&rsquo;re all yours to explore when you take a cruise to Belize, where surprises await around every corner, including underwater. Whether mountain biking through a lush rainforest or snorkeling with the marine life, you&rsquo;ll experience things you can only imagine&hellip; that is, if you haven&rsquo;t tried a Belize vacation yet.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>The Cayo District is where you&rsquo;ll find an impressive system of underground rivers and caves.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Go exploring, old-school-style, with local ancient ruins Cahal Pech, Altun Ha, or Xuananunich.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy snorkeling on this hemisphere&rsquo;s largest barrier reef.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-belize-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CAS', 'name': 'Cairns', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'cairns', 'desc_html': '<p>Visit the coastal city of Cairns and enjoy a smorgasbord of fun and adventure. A Carnival Cruise Line holiday to Cairns offers the perfect mix of shore excursions the whole family will love - on water and land. Daintree Rainforest tours are the ideal way to experience the ecosystem of the wet tropics of Queensland (a UNESCO World Heritage Site). Go snorkelling on the Great Barrier Reef, experience the Kuranda Scenic Railway and Skyrail, or have a tropical rainforest nature park adventure. A day trip to Cairns itself is always worth it, with amazing shopping on the Esplanade and scenic walks that will blow you away. </p><p>Experience stunning far North Queensland:</p>\n    <ul class="features-list">\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Browse the numerous art galleries and restaurants.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Discover the local cultural and historical sites.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Visit Cooktown, which is home to the ‘James Cook Museum’.\n    </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/AU/Cairns-Green-Sea-Turtle-on-Coral-Reef-v1-1920x1080-jpg.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CAT', 'name': 'Catalina Island', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'catalina-island', 'desc_html': 'Discover a sunny Southern California playground hidden beyond the Los Angeles horizon, on a Carnival cruise to Catalina Island. Just 22 miles from the mainland, Catalina Island has long been a getaway for savvy city hikers, sun-seekers… and film crews looking for a slice of accessible paradise. Access the breathtaking views from up high on the island’s rugged cliffs, or way down low as you snorkel or scuba the Pacific Ocean waters at Avalon Beach. Cruises to Catalina Island give you a rare opportunity to see California as it once was — from the seaside town of Avalon and tiny Two Harbors, to the undeveloped parkland of Catalina’s interior.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>While the time away with wild buffalo, on Catalina Island’s interior roads.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Snorkel through thick kelp forests at Casino Point Marine Park.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Glide into protected coves and hidden beaches by kayak.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-mexico-itinerary-catalina-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CAY', 'name': 'Grand Cayman', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'grand-cayman', 'desc_html': 'Cruise to Grand Cayman, go barefoot in the sand and be oh-so- elegant... all in one day. Enjoy laid-back British civility in a sun-splashed Caribbean tropical locale on your Carnival Grand Cayman cruise. Don’t let the island’s scrubland terrain fool you — a spectacular marine paradise lies just offshore, where a living undersea wall tapers off dramatically into the ocean depths. Cruises to Grand Cayman bring you directly to the best scuba diving and snorkeling in the kaleidoscopic Cayman Islands. When you get up close and personal with the resident stingrays and turtles, you’ll soon learn why beach-goers and nature lovers rank cruises to the Grand Cayman as some of the best in the Caribbean.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stretch out on the glimmering white sands at Seven Mile Beach.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll the shops, cafes, and museums in George Town, Grand Cayman.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>You don&rsquo;t just go to the stingrays &mdash; they come right up to you &mdash; at Stingray City.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>There&rsquo;s more than just turtles &mdash; but oh, are there turtles &mdash; at Cayman Turtle Farm..</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-grand-cayman-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CBK', 'name': 'Celebration Key™', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'celebration-key', 'desc_html': '<p>\nIt\'s time to check out Celebration Key —\xa0 a new exclusive destination from Carnival, nestled on the south side of Grand Bahama island, that\'s designed for Carnival guests. It’s perfect for adults, families with kids… everybody who appreciates fun and natural beauty.\xa0Get ready for unforgettable experiences like a mile-long white sand beach, the largest freshwater lagoons in the Caribbean<sup style="line-height: 11px;">†</sup> and five “portals” for you to\xa0enjoy.\xa0\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        <strong>Paradise Plaza</strong><span class="tradeStyling" aria-hidden="true">™</span> will be the first portal to explore, welcoming you ashore with guest information, live music, photo ops and more. <strong>Starfish Lagoon</strong><span class="tradeStyling" aria-hidden="true">™</span> is made for families — and kids of all ages — with Flash Flamingo and Mach III Marlin waterslides, Guppy Grotto splash pad, and a selection of sports courts offering basketball, beach volleyball and pickleball action. <strong>Calypso Lagoon</strong><span class="tradeStyling" aria-hidden="true">™</span> is designed for adults ready to relax... or go for more of an active vibe, with lagoon-side swim-up and swings bars, a DJ island and more. <strong>Pearl Cove Beach Club</strong><span class="tradeStyling" aria-hidden="true">™</span> welcomes adults — and only adults — to take paradise to the next level with great ocean views, infinity pool, swim-up bar, elevated dining, plus attentive service poolside or beachside. <strong>Lokono Cove</strong><span class="tradeStyling" aria-hidden="true">™</span> offers goods from local artisans, plus showcases Bahamian art, music, history and culture.\xa0\n    </p>\n<sup>†</sup> <span style="font-size:12px;"> Based on publicly available data of surface area measurements as of 01/22/25.</span><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Paradise Plaza greets you with live music and helps you find your way to all the fun that’s still to come… like maybe that Suncastle in the distance?</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>The atmosphere at Calypso Lagoon is lively… and chill! This adult-friendly portal features a swim-up bar, dining spots, a DJ island, plus plenty of ways to relax.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Starfish Lagoon is perfect for kids, teens and families, featuring a splash pad, sports courts, designated beach, dining spots, game pavilion and more. </li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Pearl Cove Beach Club is the adults-only spot that takes luxury to the next level with an infinity pool, private beach access, elevated dining, the best views of Bahamian waters and more.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em> The Retail Portal, known as Lokono Cove, is a colorful showcase of Bahamian culture featuring local art, live music and flavors, plus artisanal goods, duty-free jewelry and more great shopping. </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-bahamas-itinerary-celebration-key-21.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CFU', 'name': 'Corfu', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'corfu', 'desc_html': 'The lush and verdant island of Corfu is midway between Greece and Italy, and there lies a long and colorful history. First colonized by settlers from the city-state of Corinth, Corfu has been ruled by the Romans, the Venetians, the French and the English. Whew! Corfu today boasts fortresses bearing the insignia of the Venetian Republic, a lavish esplanade planted by the French during the Napoleonic Wars, and even an English cricket pitch. The island also offers some of the finest coastal scenery in the entire Mediterranean.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Discover the deep blue Ionian Sea from the wonderful jagged coastline of Palaiokastritsa.</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>See the Old Town section of Corfu, a UNESCO World Heritage site, featuring Venetian forts and neo-classical housing.</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy the Esplanade park and elegant Liston, which were once only open to aristocrats, but today welcome all.</li>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-corfu-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CGN', 'name': 'Cartagena', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'cartagena', 'desc_html': 'Considering cruises to Colombia? You&rsquo;ll want to make sure Cartagena is at the top of your vacation list. If you tell someone you&rsquo;re planning on visiting Cartagena, make sure you tell &lsquo;em which one &mdash; Colombia&rsquo;s fifth-largest city found its namesake in a town in Spain that&rsquo;s over 2,000 years old. But Carnival&rsquo;s cruises to Colombia take you to Cartagena, Jr. &mdash; only about 500 years young &mdash; where you&rsquo;ll find a vibrant Colombian city with a range of neighborhoods like the bustling Downtown, the traditional Getseman&iacute;, and even the waterfront Bocagrande&hellip; an entire cultural center on a walkable peninsula featuring beaches, shopping and nightlife galore. Put yourself at the center of all this action with one of Carnival&rsquo;s cruises to Cartagena.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Like many old towns, Cartagena has an &ldquo;Old Town&rdquo; section &mdash; a walled historic neighborhood you shouldn&rsquo;t miss.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Built by the Spanish for protection from pirates, Castillo de San Felipe today opens its doors warmly to visitors from all over.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>To go upscale, head downsouth. Bocagrande is home to shops, restaurants, shops and art galleries.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-panama-canal-itinerary-cartagena-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CGP', 'name': 'Cartagena', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'cartagena', 'desc_html': 'Considering cruises to Colombia? You&rsquo;ll want to make sure Cartagena is at the top of your vacation list. If you tell someone you&rsquo;re planning on visiting Cartagena, make sure you tell &lsquo;em which one &mdash; Colombia&rsquo;s fifth-largest city found its namesake in a town in Spain that&rsquo;s over 2,000 years old. But Carnival&rsquo;s cruises to Colombia take you to Cartagena, Jr. &mdash; only about 500 years young &mdash; where you&rsquo;ll find a vibrant Colombian city with a range of neighborhoods like the bustling Downtown, the traditional Getseman&iacute;, and even the waterfront Bocagrande&hellip; an entire cultural center on a walkable peninsula featuring beaches, shopping and nightlife galore. Put yourself at the center of all this action with one of Carnival&rsquo;s cruises to Cartagena.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Like many old towns, Cartagena has an &ldquo;Old Town&rdquo; section &mdash; a walled historic neighborhood you shouldn&rsquo;t miss.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Built by the Spanish for protection from pirates, Castillo de San Felipe today opens its doors warmly to visitors from all over.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>To go upscale, head downsouth. Bocagrande is home to shops, restaurants, shops and art galleries.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-panama-canal-itinerary-cartagena-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CHA', 'name': 'Charlottetown, PE', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'charlottetown', 'desc_html': 'Even the smallest of provinces have a capital city, and Charlottetown serves that role for Prince Edward Island. Canada’s littlest actually had an outsized role in the country’s history — you could basically call this the birthplace of Canada! This happened at a conference in 1864 at Province House, which is still home to the Prince Edward Island’s legislature. But that’s far from the only historic building you’ll find here — among the Victorian architecture is a humble farmhouse that you might not guess inspired the beloved children’s novel Anne of Green Gables… except that Anne fans flock there today and it’s been made a National Historic Site! But with all the talk of buildings, don’t miss the outdoors — PEI and its namesake national park play host to incredible hiking, biking and white-sand beach strolling.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-port-charlottetown-prince-edward-island-itinerary-2.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CIV', 'name': 'Civitavecchia (Rome)', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'civitavecchia-rome', 'desc_html': 'In ancient times it was said that all roads lead to Rome&hellip; but in your case, the seaport of Civitavecchia is your road to Rome. Get there and you&rsquo;ll find out what made the place so popular. The Vatican\'s Sistine Chapel by Michelangelo, the Colosseum with its lurid history, and the Trevi Fountain &mdash; where a tossed coin promises your return &mdash; are not to be missed on any visit to the so-called &ldquo;Eternal City,&rdquo; one of the cradles of civilization. Take a walking tour of Rome&rsquo;s many historical landmarks and enjoy the lively sidewalk caf&eacute;s, ending the day alla romana strolling through the atmospheric Centro Storico.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Look up at Michelangelo&rsquo;s frescos on the Sistine Chapel&rsquo;s ceiling.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Climb to the top of St. Peter&rsquo;s Basilica dome for panoramic views of Rome.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Have your picture taken on the flowery Spanish Steps.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-rome-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CLL', 'name': 'Callao (Lima)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'callao-lima', 'desc_html': 'Cruise to Callao and you\'re just 45 minutes from Lima. This \xa0megalopolis was once known as the "city of kings," but today could just be called "the city of Peruvians," since about a third of the country lives here. Lima is also a fascinating look into the two sides of Peru: the sleek and modern, and the old-world, the latter of which is still present on the streets, especially in the\xa016th century colonial architecture near Plaza de Armas,\xa0and the iconic palaces of the Government and Archbishop, both off Plaza Mayor. Even pre-colonial sights are there to see if you know where to look. Where to look, then? Visit Huaca Pucllana, a sprawling pyramid built with bricks made from earth and clay, and the fortress of the Pachacamac, both of which are thousands of years old… even dating back to a time before the Inca people. To explore Lima\'s more modern pleasures, the Barranco district brings together galleries, boutiques, top coffee and great outdoor spaces for a stroll.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-south-america-itinerary-callao-lima-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CLN', 'name': 'Colón (Panama Canal)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'colon-panama-canal', 'desc_html': 'Some see Col&oacute;n as the gateway city to the Panama Canal, the engineering wonder linking the Atlantic and Pacific oceans. Others know it as the second-largest duty-free port in all of the Caribbean, and a great base for exploring the canal and Panama&rsquo;s nearby ecological treasures. On your Carnival cruise to Col&oacute;n, you&rsquo;ll see it from all sides &mdash; enjoy a side of shop-&lsquo;till-you-drop as you spy the brilliant plumage of a toucan in rainforest greenery.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Kayak the Panama Canal in man-made Gat&uacute;n Lake.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Feast your eyes on the fetching harbor town of Portobelo.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit two oceans in one hour by traveling the Isthmian Railroad, the world\'s first trans-continental railroad.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-panama-canal-itinerary-colon-4.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CMZ', 'name': 'Costa Maya', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'costa-maya', 'desc_html': 'Cruise to Costa Maya for an irresistible blend of serene beaches, action-packed activities and the best flavors south of the border. Mexico&rsquo;s vivid Caribbean coast will appear just beyond the dock when your Carnival cruise visits Costa Maya. Silver dolphins, bright yellow angelfish, turquoise waves, ivory sand &mdash; these are just some selections from Costa Maya&rsquo;s palette that you can expect to see on your Carnival Costa Maya adventure. Inland from the port are more brilliant hues, from the otherworldly shades of blue at the Lake of Seven Colors to the white stone pyramids of the ancient Maya. This bounty of beauty is yours to explore when you cruise to Costa Maya.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Peek under the surface with the partially-excavated Chacchoben ruins.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Get your wheels spinning with vehicle options like bikes, ATVs and more.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Scuba dive with moray eels and docile nurse sharks in the Great Mesoamerican Reef.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-mexico-itinerary-costa-maya-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'COB', 'name': 'Cobh (Cork)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'cobh-cork', 'desc_html': 'When the city crest and motto is Latin for “a safe harbor for ships,” you know you’ve sailed into friendly waters. This is true of Cork, Ireland, the island’s third largest city, and coincidentally, home to the second largest natural harbor in the world. Foodies can rejoice here, as Cork has also been dubbed Ireland&rsquo;s gastro capital. Those hoping for a bit of that “luck of the Irish” can make their way to Blarney Castle to kiss the Blarney stone and put its powers to the test. No matter which route you take, timeless beauty and unique, hearty flavors await you in Cork.\n', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-cork-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CPH', 'name': 'Copenhagen', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'copenhagen', 'desc_html': 'Kick off your Carnival cruise from a city rich in history and beautiful architecture: Copenhagen. Originally a Viking village and rebuilt during the Danish Golden Age, Copenhagen is filled with beautiful architecture, scenic canals, royal castles and ancient history to behold. Glide through the city&rsquo;s canals before your cruise and admire the colorful gabled houses, cobbled streets and quaint cafes of the Christianshavn neighborhood. Become captivated at the Amalienborg Palace, the official residence of the Danish royal family, the world&rsquo;s oldest monarchy. If you&rsquo;re a foodie, savor a host of different cuisines in the city&rsquo;s popular Tivoli Gardens, known for its lush pleasure garden, historical museums and the world&rsquo;s most visited seasonal theme park.<ul class="features-list">\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Experience the changing of the Royal Guard at Amalienborg Palace before you cruise from Copenhagen.</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Go shopping at Stroget, one of Europe\'s longest pedestrian shopping streets.</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the famous sculpture of The Little Mermaid, a gift to the city of Copenhagen.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-copenhagen-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CQQ', 'name': 'Coquimbo (La Serena)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'coquimbo-la-serena', 'desc_html': "It's hard to discuss Coquimbo without also talking about nearby La Serena. The seaport city of Coquimbo certainly has impressive sights of its own, like the beautiful mosque with\xa0colorful interior details, the 300-foot brutalist\xa0Cruz del Tercer Milenio, which offers incredible views… and yes, even the local fish market! But over in nearby La Serena\xa0— which is actually a popular vacation destination for Chileans — you'll find great reasons to make the side-trip: restored buildings from the Spanish colonial period, a 19th-century cathedral, the local archaeological museum and more. Plus, you won't want to miss Chile's famous local wines, harvested nearby in the region's Elqui Valley.", 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-south-america-itinerary-coquimbo-la-serena-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CSL', 'name': 'Cabo San Lucas', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'cabo-san-lucas', 'desc_html': 'If you&rsquo;re looking for a beautiful cruise destination to call your own, cruises to Cabo San Lucas should be at the top of your list. You&rsquo;ll return home with spectacular vacation photos that get all the Likes! Cabo San Lucas makes its home on the Baja California peninsula, the second longest in the world, sitting pretty down at the south end. Tucked between golf courses and desert mountains, Cabo San Lucas straddles two oceans &mdash; the calm turquoise Sea of Cortez and the crashing blue Pacific. With 18 pristine miles of coastline connecting your port to colonial San Jos&eacute; del Cabo, you get two seaside cities in one on a Cabo San Lucas cruise. But, along with water-based activities like fishing, paddling and swimming, you can also add action &mdash; or maximum relaxation &mdash; to your itinerary. Cruises to Cabo San Lucas offer a huge variety of things to do, from riding ATVs in the desert to sipping margaritas on the beach. Try one or try it all!<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Paddle past the famous El Arco rock arch on a kayak.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Sip icy margaritas at a cantina on Playa El Medano.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Watch whopper marlin and yellowfin tuna in the Sea of Cortez.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Drive an ATV through the desert to the Candelaria oasis.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-mexico-itinerary-cabo-san-lucas-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CTA', 'name': 'Catania, Sicily', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'catania-sicily', 'desc_html': 'There’s a famous centuries-old quote about how important Sicily is — basically, if you skip it when visiting Italy, you might as well have just stayed home. We don’t exactly agree, but we know where the guy was coming from. Catania is the island’s second-largest city and an excellent place to kick off an exploration of Sicily. There’s no missing the gigantic Mt. Etna volcano — really, it’s impossible since it literally overshadows much of the island’s eastern region, and Catania puts you right in a primo position to see it. Compared to Etna, historical sites from Greek and Roman times are <em>only</em> a couple-thousand years old, but you can see them all — and some are even still in use today, like the amphitheater in Siracusa. Piazza Armerina features a villa once home to a Roman emperor, and today a UNESCO World Heritage Site, one that’s still decked out in well-preserved mosaics. Also, don’t miss the nearby town of Savoca, which you actually may have already seen… in a famous mobster trilogy. <em>Capiche?</em><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Find beautiful relaxation in Taormina — plus tons of Greek and Roman history.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Check the unique elephant sculpture adorning the town fountain of Catania.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Sample and savor the food and wine scene in Sicily, consisting of Greek, French, Arab and Spanish influences.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-catania-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CUR', 'name': 'Curaçao', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'curacao', 'desc_html': 'Cruises to Curacao take you into the exciting pulse of the Southern Caribbean. Cura&ccedil;ao is where Europe meets the West Indies, and it collides here beautifully in a smashing blend of bold colors and cosmopolitan culture. The largest of what was once the Netherlands Antilles, this Caribbean island has it all. Cruise to Cura&ccedil;ao for the beautiful beaches and historic architecture, but don&rsquo;t miss everything from the splashy sights of marine parks to the distinctive local liqueur &mdash; it all awaits on cruises to Cura&ccedil;ao. Above all, what awaits you is the warm, welcoming embrace you&rsquo;ll start to feel the minute you set sail to Cura&ccedil;ao.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take a trolley tour through the pastel-hued streets of Willemstad.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop for quality European goods and Dutch treats in the Punda District.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll across historic Queen Emma Pontoon Bridge.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the Hato Caves, a dramatic collection of grottos filled with stalactites, stalagmites and crystal clear pools.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-curacao-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'CZM', 'name': 'Cozumel', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'cozumel', 'desc_html': 'Cozumel is proof that Mexico can do &lsquo;island flavor&rsquo; with the best of the Caribbean. It may not be the biggest island in the sea, but Cozumel offers a huge variety of things to do, see, taste and explore. This island just happens to be perched atop a coral reef, which promises hours of snorkeling or scuba diving fun. Cruises to Cozumel dock at the island&rsquo;s heart &mdash; just minutes from San Miguel&rsquo;s seafront shops and the white sand beach at Chankanaab National Park. Drift among star corals and sea fans on a Cozumel diving excursion or simply kick back on the beach beneath your own palm palapa as the turquoise waves roll in. With non-stop zip line action, ancient discoveries at the nearby Mayan ruins, or time spent with your toes in the sand, a cruise to Cozumel may just top your best vacations list&hellip; before you even get home.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Cruise to Cozumel for a scuba diving adventure along the Great Mesoamerican Reef.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy a leisurely day of snorkeling with iridescent fish at Chankanaab National Park.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Swim with the flippy guys at Dolphinaris. </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-port-cozumel-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'DBV', 'name': 'Dubrovnik', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'dubrovnik', 'desc_html': 'Dubrovnik is a beautiful stone jewel, a feather in the cap of the Adriatic Sea. This picture-perfect medieval walled city boasts ancient stone buildings, narrow cobbled streets and fortified ramparts rising above red-tiled rooftops. As a Middle Ages trading center, Dubrovnik was once actually a seaport rival to Venice. Today, the city&rsquo;s amazing history is reflected in its many monuments and museums. Explore the man-made treasures like Old Town and the city&rsquo;s famous wall, but don\'t miss the natural pleasures like Dubrovnik&rsquo;s nearby beaches. A UNESCO World Heritage Site, the Old Town remains the world-renown pride of the Republic of Croatia.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Walk along the sturdy ramparts of the old walls, dating back to the 13th century.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Buy therapeutic herbs from the Franciscan Monastery&rsquo;s 14th-century apothecary.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Find holy relics and the remains of St. Blaise inside Dubrovnik Cathedral.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-dubrovnik-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'DC1', 'name': 'Cross International Date Line', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'cross-international-date-line', 'desc_html': 'Can you time-travel on a cruise? We would have to answer... "Not really, but also kind of yes!" That\'s because when you cross the International Date Line — located at the Pacific Ocean\'s own longitude 180° — you\'re sailing back in time. (Or forward, depending on which direction you\'re headed.) It instantly becomes yesterday or tomorrow, a full 24-hour jump, and just for a moment you\'re not in either the Eastern or Western hemispheres. On the ship, we mark this occasion with a unique ceremony, and you\'ll head home with a certificate to prove you experienced it.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/regions/carnival-international-date-line-2.jpg'},
    {'code': 'DLI', 'name': 'Dun Laoghaire (Dublin)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'dun-laoghaire-dublin-ireland', 'desc_html': 'Enjoy a day in emerald Ireland’s buzzing capital city of Dublin, where there’s always a song to sing, a joke to tell, and a pint to sink. Your Carnival cruise will take you to Dún Laoghaire, a buzzing town nearby with beautiful seaside views. From there it’s a short ride to laid-back yet lively Dublin, crammed with a history of revolutionaries and literary heroes that dates back at least a millennium and a half. Since the city sustained Gaelic, Viking, Norman, and English invasions during all this time, you can see the influences of all these cultures. Immerse yourself in this storied past as you stroll through Georgian terraces on Merrion Square, near Ireland’s National Gallery, where Picasso paintings compete with Jack Yeats’ Irish landscapes. Browse for local cheeses and organic wines at the Temple Bar market or enjoy some lounging on the lush St. Stephen’s Green.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-dublin-dun-laoghaire-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'DOM', 'name': 'Dominica', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'dominica', 'desc_html': 'Cruises to Dominica are full of nature&rsquo;s best, and they feature some of the Caribbean&rsquo;s most vivid waterfalls, hot springs, mountains and streams... all bubbling with life. Thrill to the sweeping grandeur of this verdant island, where wispy clouds swirl around velvety mountains and the air is alive with birdcall. On your Carnival cruise to Dominica, go wild in the lush terrain on a rainforest hike or a go native in a waterfall pool. You&rsquo;ll spot flora and fauna of every brilliant rainbow color on cruises to Dominica, from the iridescent peacocks in Papillote Gardens to giant ferns along jungle trails.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Hike to the sparkling waterfall pool of tall Middleham Falls, set deep in a rainforest.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop for straw and coconut crafts in Dominica’s Old Market Plaza, in Roseau.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Float through the treetops on the Rain Forest Aerial Tram.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-dominica-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'DOP', 'name': 'Amber Cove', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'amber-cove', 'desc_html': '<p>Discovering new sights is one of the beauties of travel, and that couldn\'t be more true when it comes to Amber Cove®, Dominican Republic. In this world full of information on just about everything, Amber Cove is a throwback &mdash; it&rsquo;s the kind of quiet little spot you won&rsquo;t find on most maps. But you will find it &mdash; brimming with bars and pools, plus opportunities for lounging and shopping &mdash; to be the gateway to island paradise, Dominican-style. Beyond Amber Cove is Puerto Plata, a town that began life as the first European settlement in the Americas. Its founder? Oh, just a guy named Christopher Columbus&hellip; so you know that arriving by sea is the ultimate way to get here. Whether you\'re looking for a day at the beach, some Dominican Republic adventure or just a little poolside me-time, Amber Cove is just the ticket.&nbsp;</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore Fort San Felipe, originally built to ward off pirates, which today welcomes curious travelers of all kinds.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>This spot is known for its remarkable local amber &mdash; actually the clearest you&rsquo;ll find anywhere in the world.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take a ride on the wild side on an amazing ATV Adventure tour through the undiscovered Dominican Republic backcountry!</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Swim with dolphins, stingrays &mdash; and yes, even sharks! &mdash; at Ocean World.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-amber-cove-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'DRW', 'name': 'Darwin', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'darwin', 'desc_html': 'Cruise across the Top End in style with a Carnival Darwin cruise. Enjoy a cruise to Darwin, and make the most of everything the laid-back capital of the Northern Territory has to offer. Take in the city’s beaches, buzzing markets and stunning air conditioned restaurants and cafes. With a Darwin cruise you can also enjoy the marinas, jetties and waterfront parks that have made the city so popular with visitors.<br /><br />\n\nAnd don’t miss the city’s amazing natural beauty, including the Charles Darwin National Park, almost alongside the Darwin cruise terminal. The fun and adventure will start before you get there, with more than 45 activities onboard a Darwin cruise, helping you make memories that will last a lifetime. Darwin is a city built for outdoor people. When you\'re not exploring on shore, Carnival\'s ships offer more than 45 onboard activities to keep the fun going between ports. Once ashore from your Darwin cruise, the options open up quickly.<br /><br />\n\nHead out on a jumping crocodile cruise along the Adelaide River, just 65 km from Darwin\'s port, one of the most exhilarating wildlife encounters in Australia, with saltwater crocodiles launching themselves from the water for bait on a stick. For something more serene, the Darwin Botanic Gardens are a shaded green sanctuary of tropical palms, cycads and flowering trees, a world away from the city\'s hum, and free to enter. Families will love Crocosaurus Cove on Mitchell Street, where you can step into the Cage of Death, a perspex cylinder lowered into a tank with a saltwater crocodile. It sounds terrifying, and it is, in the best possible way. <br /><br />\n\nCulture-seekers on a Darwin cruise can book a guided Aboriginal art tour to understand the stories behind the dot paintings, crosshatch patterns and ochre works that fill Darwin\'s many commercial galleries. Day trips from the cruise terminal also reach Litchfield National Park in about 90 minutes, a jaw-dropping landscape of magnetic termite mounds, rainforest-fed waterfalls and crystal swimming holes. For history and heritage, the Fannie Bay Gaol gives an atmospheric look at Darwin\'s colonial and wartime past. What you carry home from a Darwin cruise isn\'t just a tan and a market souvenir. It\'s the electricity of the tropics, the smell of wet earth before a storm, the sound of a didgeridoo drifting across a sun-bleached park, the knowledge that somewhere north of the harbour a crocodile is watching the waterline.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Visit the Botanical Gardens.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Enjoy Darwin’s thriving arts galleries.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Become a thrill-seeker.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Marvel at the natural beauty.\n    </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/AU/DarwinCruises-Florence-Falls-Swimming-Hole-v1-1920x1080-jpg.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ECL', 'name': 'Solar Eclipse Scenic Cruising', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'solar-eclipse-scenic-cruising', 'desc_html': '<p>One of the most unique ways to view a solar eclipse is on a Carnival cruise! What makes the ship a great location? As you may have heard, some places naturally get a more complete view, or the best part of the eclipse may last even longer. So we got our astronomical charts out to make sure you&rsquo;re getting a view that isn&rsquo;t just the best, but one of the longest!\n</p>\n<ul>\n    <li> Carnival Legend\'s August 9, 2026, Carnival Sunshine\'s July 25, 2027 and Carnival Miracle\'s July 29, 2027 sailings will feature a total eclipse, where you\'ll bask in some very unusual darkness during the middle of the day, gazing at unparalleled sights at every stage of the eclipse&hellip; including totality, corona, Baily\'s beads and more.\n    </li>\n    <li>Carnival Firenze\'s February 2, 2027 sailing will experience an annular eclipse, where the moon doesn\'t cover the sun completely. These aren\'t lesser eclipses &mdash; they\'re just different! These eclipses display the unique "ring of fire" effect, where the border of the sun is still visible.\n    </li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style="font-size: 12px;">Note: We&rsquo;re making some big eclipse plans, but naturally, the weather has to cooperate too&hellip; and anywhere in the world you go, you can never really know. Still, it&rsquo;s going to be an amazing cruise, no matter what!</span>\n</p>', 'image_url': '/-/media/CCLUS/Images/solar-eclipse/solar-eclipse-itinerary-banner-2.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ENS', 'name': 'Ensenada', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'ensenada', 'desc_html': 'Thanks to its stunning coastline, Ensenada will give you plenty of postcard-worthy moments&hellip;, and it couldn&rsquo;t be easier to get there. Escape to Mexico&rsquo;s original seaside getaway with Carnival cruises to Ensenada. Once a favorite hideaway for high-rolling Hollywood stars, Ensenada is now one of Mexico&rsquo;s most popular ports of call. You can sightsee, shop or kayak at Punta Banda&hellip; but the true pleasures of this festive city are culinary. That&rsquo;s why a cruise to Ensenada, Mexico should top every foodie&rsquo;s wish list. Have your fill of fresh oysters and sip a rich Baja merlot. Soak up the richness of the local culture as you enjoy the journey.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Try unique Baja cuisine in Ensenada, the region\'s seafood and culinary capital.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop for silver jewelry and handmade pottery on Avenida L&oacute;pez Mateos.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Watch the sea spout at La Bufadora burst from the rocks on Punta Banda.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-mexico-itinerary-ensenada-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ESC', 'name': 'Crossing The Equator', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'crossing-the-equator', 'desc_html': 'For one of the most memorable experiences at sea, this destination sure doesn\'t look like much! But crossing the invisible line of Earth\'s equator has long been a fun maritime tradition, celebrated everywhere from military vessels to the merchant marines... to, yes, even cruise ships. And when we say "long," this whole thing dates back to at least the 17th\xa0century, so this connects you to a tradition you can read about in history books. Speaking of tradition, your ship will be the site of a King Neptune ceremony, where all the pollywogs graduate to become trusty shellbacks, with the certificates to prove it. (Don\'t ask…\xa0just trust us on this one.)', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/regions/carnival-equator-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'FNC', 'name': 'Funchal, Madeira', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'funchal', 'desc_html': 'Toast your cruise to Madeira, Portugal, with a glass of sweet local wine. Located over 500 miles southwest of Portugal, this paradise is a &ldquo;Garden Island&rdquo; with a mountainous volcanic landscape covered in flower&ndash;filled vegetation. Swirling mosaic&ndash;patterned pavements decorate its main city Funchal, centered on the Pra&ccedil;a do Munic&iacute;pio. It&rsquo;s easy to enjoy the sweet scents of flowers and salty sea air when you set sail on your cruise to Portugal.<ul class="features-list">\n\t<li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tAscend one mile in a cable car to Monte, overlooking the harbor and cliffs.\n\t</li>\n    <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tExperience a thrilling toboggan or &ldquo;snowless&rdquo; sled ride downhill to Livramento.\n\t</li>\n    <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tExplore the exotic specimens of local flora at Madeira Botanical Gardens.\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tStroll the Pra&ccedil;a do Munic&iacute;pio&mdash;its mosaics were made from lava rock.\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tEnjoy every detail of the lush backdrop with a leisurely drive to Camacha.\n\t</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-funchal-madeira-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'FS1', 'name': 'Fun Day At Sea', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'fun-day-at-sea', 'desc_html': 'No port today! It’s a great time to explore your ship and its exciting entertainment, food and activities! Or take it easy at the pool, spa, or... if you book a room with a balcony, enjoy the waves.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/regions/carnival-fun-day-at-sea-banner-5.jpg'},
    {'code': 'FUK', 'name': 'Fukuoka (Hakata)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'fukuoka-hakata', 'desc_html': "Hakata is overflowing with fascinating history, serene temples and spectacular scenery. Outside Hakata, Kokura Castle is surrounded by a beautiful garden where visitors can witness a traditional tea ceremony. Soak up the spectacular scenery on a gondola-like boat called a donko as you cruise along the Yanagawa River. Explore the Moji Historical District, a charming area that sits along Kyushu's waterfront boasting many interesting historic buildings.", 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/AU/Fukuoka-Tochoji-Temple-Pagoda-in-Autumn-v1-1920x1080-jpg.jpg'},
    {'code': 'GAL', 'name': 'Galveston', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'galveston', 'desc_html': 'Set sail from this historic jewel on Carnival cruises out of Galveston, Texas. Perched on the Gulf Coast, Galveston was a major commercial port in the late 1800s and has the restored architecture and proud history to show for it. Galveston’s long seawall stretches from beach to beach and offers gulf views the whole way. Sprinkle in a few museums, amusement parks, attractive beaches and tasty seafood restaurants, and you’ve got a great start to your cruise from Galveston.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop for antiques in the historic Strand District, near where Carnival cruises from Galveston dock.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Hear the sounds of a Central American rainforest at the gardens. </li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Treat yourself to spa day at a historical hotel.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Bike the length of the mural-adorned Seawall.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-galveston-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'GCI', 'name': 'St. Peter Port', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'st-peter-port', 'desc_html': 'Guernsey is part of the Channel Islands, which span the waters between France and England… although it’s technically not part of either and has a history that stretches back beyond both countries. St. Peter Port was once home to novelist Victor Hugo — and notably not Napoleon, who failed to conquer it — but today hosts a picturesque harbor, historic houses, flower-lined streets and even a castle. There are flavors to be found too, a delicious reminder of the watery crossroads of cultures that have passed through the island, bestowing it with pubs, fish and chip shops, local Roquette apple cider… not to mention the famous sweet gâche bread, a Christmas favorite.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-st-peters-port-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'GDT', 'name': 'Grand Turk', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'grand-turk', 'desc_html': 'Let the name fool you &mdash; Grand Turk, of the Turks &amp; Caicos islands, may be small but it&rsquo;s packed with scenic punch and historic charm. Carnival cruises to Grand Turk deliver you to this enchanted island outpost dotted with old windmills, grassy trails and picture-perfect beaches. Discover an oasis of green set in aquamarine seas, ringed by a pristine coral reef and the steep wall of the continental shelf.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Swim in the sparkling turquoise seas off Governor&rsquo;s Beach.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour historic Cockburn Town and the old salt pans.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop for duty-free jewelry and local crafts in the colorful Grand Turk Cruise Center.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Feel the velvety touch of a stingray&rsquo;s wings in Gibbs Cay.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-grand-turk-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'GIB', 'name': 'Gibraltar', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'gibraltar', 'desc_html': 'Best known as the gateway to the Mediterranean, Gibraltar is a port whose big features defy its reputation as a tiny British territory. For instance, the Rock of Gibraltar is more a mountain than a pebble &mdash; despite its understated name &mdash; and features limestone burrow tunnels that helped Gibraltar fend off invaders for over 200 years. The most scenic way up the rock is the Mediterranean Steps &mdash; imagine a staircase leading up the great rock towards even greater vistas. Down below in Gibraltar (and especially on Main Street) shopping is big&hellip; and perhaps more importantly, it&rsquo;s duty-free.<ul class="features-list">\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Traverse the elaborate network of World War II tunnels still in existence in Gibraltar.</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Pause for a photo op at Europa Point’s famous red and white lighthouse.</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Make St. Michael’s Cave your new top spot, with its stalagmites, stalactites, underground passageways and amphitheater.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-gibraltar-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'GLA', 'name': 'Greenock (Glasgow)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'greenock-glasgow', 'desc_html': 'Quick Scotland lesson: the country is divided into the Lowlands and Highlands, and while it sounds like a matter of elevation… they basically just mean the north part and the south! Glasgow could be thoughts of the capital of the Lowlands region, plus it’s the third most populated city in all of the U.K. It’s one of the top spots to survey Victorian-era architecture — castles and cathedrals abound — with a few choice selections even surviving from the medieval period. Glasgow is a museum lover’s dream, boasting countless collections dedicated to beautiful art… and even other interesting pursuits like the Glasgow Museum of Transport.<ul class="features-list">\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Walk Glasgow’s oldest house and gardens, Provand\'s Lordship, dating back to the 1400s.</li>\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See dinosaurs, suits of armor — oh, and art — at Kelvingrove Art Gallery and Museum.</li>\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Unlock great views of some of Scotland’s incredible lochs: Loch Lomond, Loch Eck and Holy Loch.</li>\r\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-glasgow-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'GOA', 'name': 'Genoa', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'genoa', 'desc_html': "The city has been declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site, but that might not even be one of the most interesting things about Genoa! You can't miss the local flavor — this region being the birthplace of pesto, why pass up a chance to try it from the source? Dining and shopping are two great pastimes here, but a house that's said to be the birthplace of Christopher Columbus may compete for your attention, while spectacular cathedrals and palaces pack plenty of medieval appeal. But sometimes it's the space between the buildings that counts, and Via Giuseppe Garibaldi, a street that dates back to the Renaissance, shows up in the works of Charles Dickens, and is home to gardens and at least 42 palaces. Some of these welcomed notable visitors in the 16th and 17th centuries, and many of the palaces today have a home on\xa0that UNESCO list.", 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-genoa-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'GOT', 'name': 'Gothenburg', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'gothenburg', 'desc_html': 'Gothenburg is the second largest city in Sweden, but comes in first when you\'re looking at the biggest seaports across of all the Nordic countries. Located on the west coast, at the mouth of the G&#246;ta &#228;lv river, Gothenburg features a great assortment of elegance — everything from castles to canals to stylish buildings. For a bit of city culture, visit G&#246;taplatsen, where a bronze statue of Poseidon and its fountain sit in the central square along with the city’s museum and concert hall. Or seize the opportunity to slow things down with a short boat ride to the southern archipelago. The very small islands don’t allow cars, giving life a much gentler pace. For residents, days consist of fishing, sailing and other marine activities… but even for someone like you who\'s just dropping in, a visit can make you feel worlds away from city life.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>\n\tCatch an ocean view… from a castle! Head to the peninsula and indulge in the 16th century Gothic style.\n\t</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>\n\tTake a scenic ride on the canals of the city for a memorable experience.\n\t</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>\n\tShop the small stuff — the city center is a cornucopia of independent vintage and couture clothing shops, electronics stores and more.\n\t</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-gothenburg-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'GPE', 'name': 'Guadeloupe', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'guadeloupe', 'desc_html': 'Of all the Lesser Antiles, Guadeloupe is among the greatest&hellip; and it&rsquo;s about as fun as it is French. And yes, it&rsquo;s totally French. The island group also has the title of largest European Union territory in North America. (Now you know!) Guadeloupe&rsquo;s size gives you many opportunities to explore and see why the island group is called &ldquo;Pearl of the French Caribbean.&rdquo; As the name might suggest, Grande-Terre is one of the biggest islands of the pearl, and Sainte-Anne is the most popular resort town you&rsquo;ll find anywhere in Guadeloupe. Not far away you&rsquo;ll find Fleur d &rsquo;Ep&eacute;e, a fort whose elevation provides superior views of the island&hellip; and some of its islandy neighbors. And for our final installment of <em>Local Fun You Can&rsquo;t Pronounce</em>, Cascades des Ecrevisses in Guadeloupe National Park proves that a splashy natural wading pool &mdash; complete with waterfall &mdash; is actually a universal language.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take a dip at the Cascades des Ecrevisses in Guadeloupe National Park</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore the shops and beaches in the resort town of Sainte Anne</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-guadeloupe-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'HEL', 'name': 'Helsinki', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'helsinki', 'desc_html': 'When you take a Carnival cruise to Helsinki, the capital city of Finland, you’ll discover a mix of old and new. An exceptional city of design, Helsinki offers a wonderful mix of old and new, with neoclassical buildings from the 1800s that delightfully complement stunning modern architecture. Situated on the edge of a leafy peninsula in a pocket of the Baltic Sea, Helsinki has stunning geographical features such as pebbled esplanades and tree-filled parks you won’t want to miss. Experience avant-garde museums, shop for accessories and fashion and remember to bring your camera along while you’re tackling your bucket list.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Spend an afternoon at the Kiasma contemporary art museum.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit Suomenlinna, a massive 18th-century sea fortress.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Admire the beautiful neoclassical buildings of Helsinki.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit Helsinki’s leafy outskirts, where Finns have perfected enjoying the good life.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-helsinki-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'HKG', 'name': 'Hong Kong', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'hong-kong', 'desc_html': 'Imagine a shimmering forest of steel and glass skyscrapers, bustling harbor waters filled with junks and sampans, and the inviting green hills of Kowloon. Welcome to Hong Kong, a top travel destination that never fails to enchant with all its excitement and exotic charm! \n\nOn Hong Kong Island, modern skyscrapers and luxury hotels rise majestically. The narrow streets are alive with noodle vendors and fortunetellers. The countless shops offer everything from bespoke suits and ancient porcelain to the latest in consumer electronics. Over seven million people move at a dizzying pace in this vibrant hub of capitalism, commerce, and enterprise.\n\nWith so much to see and do, the hardest part will be choosing what to do first. For a breathtaking view of the entire city, head to Victoria Peak. Savor lunch at one of the city\'s famous dim sum restaurants. Stroll down the crowded streets to feel the city\'s energetic pulse. And whether you\'re in the mood or not—shop. After all, you\'re in the duty-free capital of the world!\n\n\n\n<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take in breathtaking city views from Victoria Peak</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Discover some of the world’s best shopping</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll through the bustling streets</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-asia-itinerary-hongkong-1.png'},
    {'code': 'HLY', 'name': 'Holyhead, Wales', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'holyhead', 'desc_html': 'You’ll find the town of Holyhead at the nation of Wales’ northwesternmost tip, and in one of the most dramatic lighthouse scenes available anywhere, the landmass practically points across the sea towards Ireland. Holyhead today is scenic, but actually began as strategic — the city center you can still explore was originally the site of a Roman fort. Beyond Holyhead itself lies so much Welsh beauty across the Anglesey region: verdant hills, imposing castles, historic railways, neighboring villages and more. Plus don’t miss the local arts center or the charming pubs!<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take a tram tour through the underground world of miners in Victorian times.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the world’s oldest railway company — nearly 200 years old.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour the castles Caernarfon, Beaumarais or Conwy, all 13th-century British constructions.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-holyhead-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'HMD', 'name': 'RelaxAway, Half Moon Cay™', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'relaxaway', 'desc_html': '<style>\r\n.trade_styling {\r\n  font-size: 70%;\r\n  position: relative;\r\n  top: -0.3em;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\nAfter you see the pristine beaches and breathtaking turquoise waters, it’s no surprise that Half Moon Cay was named Best Private Island... for more than 20 straight years! And now the destination has expanded with not only more tropical tranquility, but new ways to spend your paradise-time. That\'s why we\'re now calling it RelaxAway, Half Moon Cay!\r\n<br /><br />\r\nSet sail on a Carnival cruise to this exclusive destination, arriving by pier or water shuttle, and from your first step onto the sand you’ll understand why it’s anything but typical. All the excitement aboard your Carnival cruise pauses for a bit, opening up your vacation to a truly effortless private island escape.\r\n<br /><br />\r\nStroll a scenic nature path or cozy up and lounge with your someone special in a daybed, a shady hideaway for two. If you’re looking for more private stretch out space, there are rental cabanas and villas too. You know, kicking back is encouraged at RelaxAway, Half Moon Cay… but against this lush backdrop there’s still so much to do. Play in turquoise seas, ride horseback along powdery white sand, or gently paddle a kayak through acres of protected lagoon, encountering silky smooth stingrays.\r\n<br /><br />\r\nAnd because a great beach day deserves great flavors, we’ve also added new complimentary lunch spots and an expanded selection of island themed bars for sipping and unwinding in paradise.\r\n<br /><br />\r\nRelaxAway, Half Moon Cay is part of the Paradise Collection<span class="trade_styling">&trade;</span> by Carnival, where each cruise destination showcases a different slice of paradise, from breathtaking, white sand beaches to vibrant cultures and unforgettable excursions.\r\n<br /><br /><style>\n    .SmileIconBullet {\n        max-width: 36px;\n        max-height: 21px;\n        position: absolute;\n        left: 0;\n    }\n    </style>\n    \n    \n    <ul class="features-list">\n        <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Compare swim strokes with the island’s gentle stingrays.</li>\n        <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Find plenty of room to enjoy nature with over one mile of white-sand beach.</li>\n        <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See the island’s incredible scenery from atop horseback.</li>\n    </ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-bahamas-relaxaway-half-moon-cay-itinerary-7.jpg'},
    {'code': 'HNL', 'name': 'Honolulu, Oahu', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'honolulu', 'desc_html': 'Whether you&rsquo;re on a cruise to Honolulu from the mainland, or a cruise from Honolulu, you&rsquo;ll find yourself spellbound by this magical Pacific destination. Before or after your cruise, take the time to explore the historic port of Honolulu and its lively mix of world-class dining, perfect beaches and lush, tropical landscape. It&rsquo;s hard to imagine a more picture-perfect holiday destination, and a cruise to Honolulu is an ideal way to experience it. Situated on the beautiful island of O&rsquo;ahu, Honolulu invites you to stroll the fabled beaches of Waikiki under the protective watch of the ancient volcanic profile of Diamond Head... or visit the Polynesian Cultural Center, a 42-acre living museum of many South Pacific cultures. And be sure to stop off at the historic USS Arizona Memorial, an important landmark dedicated to those who lost their lives at Pearl Harbor.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Experience an authentic luau, complete with traditional imu ceremony.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Learn about Hawaiian life &mdash; and the larger &lsquo;neighborhood&rsquo; of Polynesia &mdash; at the educational and entertaining Polynesian Cultural Center.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>There&rsquo;s more to Honolulu than great beaches &mdash; see the historic buildings that make up this bustling state capital.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-hawaii-itinerary-honolulu-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'HUX', 'name': 'Huatulco', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'huatulco', 'desc_html': 'Where the Sierra Madre del Sur mountains meet the Pacific Ocean, you’ll find a charming resort town that boasts an incredible natural bounty: nine bays and so many beaches — dozens! — that the idea of a crowded beach become an impossibility. While Huatulco is well-equipped to welcome visitors, much of the area has been critically set aside for nature reserves… in this rainforest-rich destination you’re never far from the best of either of these worlds. The nearby Copalita River and its over 200 species is a birdwatcher’s paradise, plus there’s relics dating back to 500 B.C. still being uncovered at an archaeological site. The nearby artisanal town of La Crucecita features a verdant plaza-park that’s a local crossroads, and a church that’s home to an impressive edge-to-edge ceiling mural. Regional Oaxacan cuisine is among Mexico’s most iconic culinary exports — think tamales and tortillas — and you’ll find it’s well-worth enjoying these fresh from the source.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Lose count of just how many species of birds you’ve spotted along the lush Copalita River.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Hop from spectacular bay to spectacular bay — Santa Cruz, Tangolunda, Chahue, Organo are just a few great spots to see the sand meet the Pacific Ocean.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Catch a cooking demonstration of local delicacies at community kitchen Piedra de Moros.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Discover Mexico’s largest ecological reserve alongside stunning beaches at Bahia de Huatulco.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-panama-canal-port-huatulco-3.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ITO', 'name': 'Hilo, Hawaii', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'hilo', 'desc_html': 'Nestled on the slopes of volcanic Mauna Loa, the port of Hilo offers visitors a path on which to step back in time. Your Carnival cruise to Hilo alohas you to low-key Hawaii, where island life moves at a slower pace, people still greet each other on the street and blossoming flowers and macadamia thrive, all to the delight of the senses. A Hilo cruise transports you to this Hawaiian town draped in lush tropical foliage, overlooking the placid waters of Hilo Bay.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Meander among the trees of Banyan Drive.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See a slice of 19th-century life in the Lyman Museum &amp; Mission House.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Experience a tsunami safely &mdash; without even getting wet &mdash; at the Pacific Tsunami Museum.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-hawaii-itinerary-hilo-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'IZM', 'name': 'Izmir (Ephesus)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'izmir-ephesus', 'desc_html': 'Surrounded by mountains on three sides, this booming Turkish city is located on a gulf fed by several streams. Evidence of the city&rsquo;s rich culture includes the ancient fortress Kadifekale, the fountain-fitted Saat Kulesi clock tower, the ruins of the ancient downtown Agora&hellip; and, of course, the eclectic Kizlaragasi Han Bazaar. Izmir is also the gateway to Ephesus, the ancient Greek city built in the 10th century B.C. &mdash; home of the Temple of Artemis, one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Experience ancient Ephesus, considered to be one of the seven wonders of the ancient world.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the House where the Blessed Virgin is said to have spent her last years.</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>See the terrace houses, which remained buried from the 7th century until the 1980s.</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-izmir-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'JAP', 'name': 'Puntarenas', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'puntarenas', 'desc_html': 'Bordering a gentle stretch of sand kissed by Pacific breezes, the former rough-and-tumble port town of Puntarenas, Costa Rica is now a laid-back seaside retreat. With a Puntarenas cruise, you can stroll the mile-long seafront Paseo de los Turistas boardwalk past restaurants, caf&eacute;s and colorful souvenir stands. On your Carnival cruise to Puntarenas, relax on the powdery beach and watch the sun melt into the Gulf of Nicoya.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop for local crafts and rich Costa Rican coffee on Puntarenas cruises.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Watch the sunset from the Puntarenas beach.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Swing above the rainforest on a zipline canopy ride.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Listen for the call of brilliant scarlet macaws in Carara National Park.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-panama-canal-itinerary-puntarenas-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'JAX', 'name': 'Jacksonville', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'jacksonville', 'desc_html': 'Cruises from Jacksonville offer the perfect blend of beachfront and urban exploration. Get the best of a laid-back beach town and a buzzing city when you book a Carnival cruise from the beautiful port of Jacksonville, Florida. The Sunshine State&rsquo;s largest city has a redeveloped and revitalized downtown, full of upbeat shopping and lively restaurants, bisected by the scenic St. Johns River and its Southbank Riverwalk. Jacksonville is a gateway to the islands of the Bahamas but you&rsquo;ll also have 20 miles of sandy beach life and endless acres of wildlife parks to enjoy before you board your Carnival cruise from Jacksonville.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See 100-year-old gardens at the Cummer Museum of Art &amp; Gardens.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll the Jacksonville Riverwalk for views of the St. Johns.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Watch for whales from Jacksonville Beach before departing on your Carnival cruise.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit St. Augustine, the oldest European settlement in the U.S.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-jacksonville-2.jpg'},
    {'code': 'JGU', 'name': 'Grenada', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'grenada', 'desc_html': 'Cruises to Grenada are ideal for those with a taste for nature and robust flavors. Known as the &ldquo;Isle of Spice,&rdquo; Grenada definitely leaves a flavor in your memories after a visit. There&rsquo;s a reason for this, too&hellip; and it&rsquo;s more than just the island&rsquo;s role as one of the world&rsquo;s most important producers of nutmeg, cinnamon, cloves, ginger and allspice. Meshed somewhere in the tropical air, the winding rivers and the fertile soil &mdash; a result of the island&rsquo;s volcanic origins &mdash; is a life energy of a distinctly south Caribbean sort. On your Carnival cruise to Grenada, you&rsquo;ll notice it at the beaches, hear it in the reggae and calypso, and taste it in rich local delicacies&hellip; like a dish known as &ldquo;oildown&rdquo; (breadfruit and fresh fish). Treat your palate &mdash; and all of your senses &mdash; to the magic of cruises to Grenada.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Discover the historic Fort George combined with a relaxing time at Aquarium Beach Club.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See birds, monkeys and more play in the treetops at Grand Etang National Park, situated in a rainforest.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy a day of snorkeling, swimming, sailing, and lobster &lsquo;n&rsquo; champagne lunch.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the narrow streets &mdash; and amazing views &mdash; of Carenage. This little harbor offers great shopping, restaurants and bars.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-grenada-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'JNU', 'name': 'Juneau', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'juneau', 'desc_html': 'Astounding ice-capped mountains welcome the cruising traveler to Juneau. Alaska is called the Land of the Midnight Sun, and its capital shines with a wide selection of delicious dining and native Alaskan art shopping. But Juneau isn&rsquo;t just a fun name to say, you know &mdash; Carnival cruises to Juneau transport you to one of the most beautiful capital cities in America, with once-in-a-lifetime shore excursions that include walking on glaciers, whale watching, and hikes through the country&rsquo;s last old-growth forests.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See Alaska&rsquo;s history displayed at the state&rsquo;s leading museums.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Touch glacier ice that&rsquo;s thousands of years old.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll beneath the mystic green canopy of a Pacific Coast rainforest.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See the remains of what was long ago the biggest gold mine in America.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-alaska-itinerary-juneau-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'JTR', 'name': 'Santorini', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'santorini', 'desc_html': 'Thira’s the capital of the island of Santorini, and the town features a landscape of beautiful whitewashed Cycladic buildings, many iconically topped with blue domes — and all built right into the side of plunging cliffs. Such drama! Such beauty! And with views such as these, it might be hard to believe that there’s more to Santorini than its incredible photo ops. But explore deeper, because the island is packing more serious stuff, such as a winery with some of the world’s oldest vineyards, beaches decked out with spectacular black sand and even a pair of offshore islands crafted long ago by volcanic eruptions. Did we mention that back in the ’60s, archaeologists uncovered remains of a Bronze Age city that some people believe could have been Atlantis? Honestly, who knows — but really, why wouldn’t Atlanteans want to live in beautiful Santorini?', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-santorini-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'KAT', 'name': 'Katakolon (Olympia)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'katakolon-olympia', 'desc_html': 'A short distance from the fishing village and seaport of Katakolon you’ll find Olympia, where lies arguably the most important location in all of sports. It’s the site of the original Olympic Games, which went on for nearly 1,200 years, every four years, until a Roman emperor banned them in A.D. 393. The discarded ruins were uncovered only about 150 years ago — and today, Olympia’s importance is much better understood. It’s actually been declared a national park! There’s so much history on display in Olympia at the original sites, such as the Temple of Zeus, the Olympic Stadium and the Olympia Archaeological Museum, which features fine sculptures such as the “Winged Victory” statue of Nike. (Did you know she was the Greek goddess of victory?)', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-katakolon-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'KEL', 'name': 'Keelung (Taipei)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'keelung-taipei', 'desc_html': '<p>On a Carnival cruise to Taiwan, guests can explore Keelung, gateway to Taipei. A sophisticated modern metropolis that has not forgotten its rich traditional past, Taipei is the largest city and capital of Taiwan, located on the Danshui River.</p>\n\n<p>For those who love the hustle and bustle of a big city, Taipei truly is a great place to visit. It is renowned for its shopping malls, among the most popular being Taipei 101 Mall. If shopping isn&rsquo;t your thing explore the quaint, old cobblestone streets of Chiufen village or take in some history at the National Palace Museum. For something peaceful, visit the Tienlai Hot Springs Resort - nestled among the verdant slopes of Yangmingshan National Park or head to Yehliu Geographic Park, known for its otherworldly rock formations.</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour the Chiang Kai-Shek Memorial Hall</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the National Palace Museum</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore quaint Chiufen village</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Relax at the Tienlai Hot Springs Resort</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-asia-itinerary-keelung-1.png'},
    {'code': 'KET', 'name': 'Ketchikan (Ward Cove), Alaska', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'ketchikan-ward-cove', 'desc_html': 'For more than 100 years, Ketchikan, Alaska has been the gateway to the North. Ketchikan cruises dock along the famed historic waterfront. Check out the flourishing art scene and spectacular totem poles that have transformed this former frontier town into a popular southern Alaskan port of call. Experience the sights, atmosphere and excitement of the Last Frontier as soon as you cross the Alaska border on Carnival cruises to Ketchikan.\r\n<ul class="features-list">\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Catch a demonstration of lumberjacking skills by adroit woodsmen &mdash; and woodswomen.</li>\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Drop into quaint shops on a historic street that&rsquo;s actually a dock.</li>\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the Totem Heritage Center, where ancient totem poles, rescued from decay, are preserved.</li>\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Experience the Tracy Arm Wilderness Area, including exciting close-up views of the majestic Sawyer Glaciers.</li>\r\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-alaska-itinerary-ketchikan-5.jpg'},
    {'code': 'KEY', 'name': 'Key West', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'key-west', 'desc_html': 'Cruises to Key West are packed with coastal-town energy and layers of American history just waiting to be discovered.  Enjoy a laidback Caribbean vibe with a dash of the high life on Carnival cruises to Key West. The southernmost island of the Florida Keys, Key West is a sunny, fun-loving place with plenty of charm, and more than a little touristy goofiness. (But that&rsquo;s optional.) Key West cruises deliver you to palm-shaded streets lined with gaily-painted bungalows, vintage saloons and blooming tropical flowers. Whether life&rsquo;s a beach or you&rsquo;re life of the party, cruises to Key West definitely over-deliver.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll amid 19th-century architecture in Key West&rsquo;s Old Town.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Step inside the breeze-filled homes of Hemingway and Audubon.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Make a pilgrimage to the southernmost point in the United States.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Join the perpetual party in one of the town&rsquo;s old-time fisherman&rsquo;s saloons.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-bahamas-itinerary-key-west-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'KIL', 'name': 'Kiel (Hamburg)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'kiel-hamburg', 'desc_html': 'Just west of Berlin, Hamburg is one of Europe&rsquo;s largest and major ports. It sits right on the Elbe river, which is just one of its many (many!) bodies of water all around this city. So much so that it has about 2,500 bridges to cross over them, more than any other city in the world. Visit the Alster Lakes, once a water reservoir to power old mills and now a place where people come to enjoy the outdoors, you&rsquo;ll find kayaking, biking and other fun maritime activities. There is also a great deal of rich history here: The huge 18th century Church of St. Michael, with its beautiful architecture from the Baroque period is a marvel – and a great photo op. And when you&rsquo;re ready to unwind, walk down the streets of the Reeperbahn, a vibrant and well-known entertainment street in the St. Pauli district, also famous for its red light district.\n<ul class="features-list">\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Admire the beautiful canals and brick gothic of Speicherstadt, a historic UNESCO landmark from the 19th century.</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the 17th century buildings of Krameramtsstuben, which amazingly survived the bomb raids of WWII.</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop and sightsee at the grand promenade of Jungfernsteig, located along the waterfront of Binnenalster.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-port-kiel-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'KOA', 'name': 'Kona, Hawaii', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'kona', 'desc_html': 'You&rsquo;ve probably already sampled the famous local export &mdash; the coffee &mdash; so now dive deep into Hawaiian history on a Carnival cruise to Kona. While sailing the sunny, leeward side of the Big Island of Hawaii, you can tour a Hawaiian royal palace, see the first Christian church in Hawaii, and explore an ancient Hawaiian sanctuary. The black-lava coast of Kona, Hawaii, is ideal for deep sea fishing, snorkeling, scuba diving, and kayaking&mdash;all fueled with strong Kona Coast coffee.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Fish for a &ldquo;grander,&rdquo; a 1,000-pound marlin, off the Kona Coast.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Discover the island&rsquo;s royal history at Hulihee Palace.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Swim with rainbow-colored tropical fish while snorkeling during Kona cruises.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-hawaii-itinerary-kona-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'KOT', 'name': 'Kotor', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'kotor', 'desc_html': 'Have you cruised a fjord lately? Well, fjord lovers take note: Kotor rests at the edge of the largest in the south of Europe. This body of water is a thing of beauty, but there&rsquo;s more to Kotor &mdash; the city also sits at the base of an amazing mountain that makes for some dramatic overhead views. 360 degrees of beauty! How welcoming to visitors can a place be when it&rsquo;s ringed by sturdy Venetian fortress walls&hellip; ones built all the way up the mountain to keep invaders out, no less? You&rsquo;d be surprised! The old-town walled section of Kotor today throws its doors open to visitors from around the world who come to seek signs of its history among the local palaces, cathedrals and museums.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit a palace and a museum… at the same time! Montenegro’s National Museum is located in the royal palace where a king once lived.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Get top views — pun fully intended — from the vantage point of Njeguši, from which postcard-perfect photos are assured.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Say “hey” to history in Budva, one of the oldest spots you’ll find in the region, clocking in at over 2,500 years old.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-kotor-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'KTN', 'name': 'Ketchikan', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'ketchikan', 'desc_html': 'For more than 100 years, Ketchikan, Alaska has been the gateway to the North. Ketchikan cruises dock along the famed historic waterfront. Check out the flourishing art scene and spectacular totem poles that have transformed this former frontier town into a popular southern Alaskan port of call. Experience the sights, atmosphere and excitement of the Last Frontier as soon as you cross the Alaska border on Carnival cruises to Ketchikan.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Catch a demonstration of lumberjacking skills by adroit woodsmen &mdash; and woodswomen.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Drop into quaint shops on a historic street that&rsquo;s actually a dock.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the Totem Heritage Center, where ancient totem poles, rescued from decay, are preserved.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Experience the Tracy Arm Wilderness Area, including exciting close-up views of the majestic Sawyer Glaciers.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-alaska-itinerary-ketchikan-3.jpg'},
    {'code': 'KUS', 'name': 'Kusadasi (Ephesus), Turkey', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'kusadasi-ephesus-turkey', 'desc_html': 'Kusadasi is fiercely proud to show off its history, which can be traced back 5,000 years. Visitors today flock here to take it all in &mdash; the city&rsquo;s population shoots up every summer as folks from around the world come to hit the beaches, stroll the downtown shopping area and wonder at views of the iconic Kusadasi Castle, which stoically watches over the harbor from atop a small island nearby. Not far beyond Kusadasi is the ancient city of Ephesus. Nobody lives there today, but ancient residents left behind impressive signs of their civilization for posterity, including the Celsus Library, and an Amphitheater whose size rivals modern stadiums.<ul class="features-list">\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Check out the carpets here — seriously, Turkey has been known for its distinct, handwoven artisanal carpets for over 3,000 years.\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Experience ancient Ephesus, considered to be one of the seven wonders of the ancient world.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the house where the Blessed Virgin is said to have spent her last years.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-kusadasi-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LAP', 'name': 'La Paz', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'la-paz', 'desc_html': '<p>Pull into the Sea of Cortez on Carnival cruises to La Paz, Mexico. The breezy capital of Baja California Sur sits on a peaceful bay of rocky islands and secluded sandy beaches. Just below the surface, spirited sea lions and gentle whale sharks swim alongside adventurous snorkelers. Discover the vibrant underwater life of what author Jacques Cousteau once labeled the &ldquo;world&rsquo;s aquarium&rdquo; when you visit La Paz on your cruise to Mexico.</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Find hidden coves and beaches on a kayak excursion.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Dig into a plate of juicy lobster at a Tecolote beachfront restaurant.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Play with sea lions in their natural habitat when you cruise to La Paz.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-mexico-itinerary-la-paz-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LCG', 'name': 'La Coruña', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'la-coruna', 'desc_html': 'Anything dubbed the Tower of Hercules commands a bit of attention, and so does La Coruña, Spain, the site on which this iconic 180-foot-tall lighthouse stands. Located in Galicia, La Coruña is considered the third holiest site in all Christendom, attracting pilgrims in droves as they make their way to Santiago de Compostela, where St. James the Apostle is believed to have been buried. Rich in tradition and rich in celebration, Galicia is also said to be home to more than 750 beaches and host to 4,000 parties annually. If you are here to set off on a quiet retreat into the mystical, or rejoice until the nines with <em>vino</em> and <em>tapas </em>by the ocean breeze, you’re certainly in for something unforgettable at La Coruña, Spain.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-la-coruna-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LEH', 'name': 'Le Havre (Paris)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'le-havre-paris', 'desc_html': 'Sail to good&#8209;living, art&#8209;loving Normandy on Carnival cruises to Le Havre, France. Sitting pretty on France&apos;s north coast, overlooking the English Channel, Le Havre has risen from the rubble of World War II to become one of France&apos;s most dynamic port towns. Modernist architecture, Monet artworks, delicious seafood, wild cliff&#8209;backed beaches&#8209;you&apos;ll find the lot on your Le Havre cruise.\n<ul class="features-list">\n       <li>\n                 <em class="dest-check"></em>\n                See the light in the Monet masterpieces gracing Mus&eacute;e Malraux on Le Havre cruises.\n     </li>\n    <li>\n                 <em class="dest-check"></em>\n                 Snap photos of Oscar Niemeyer&apos;s volcano&#8209;shaped arts center, Le Volcan.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n                <em class="dest-check"></em>\n                Windsurf, sail or kitesurf at Le Havre&apos;s pebbly beach.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n                <em class="dest-check"></em>\n                Stand in awe of Auguste Perret&apos;s modernist monolith, &Eacute;glise St&#8209;Joseph.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n                <em class="dest-check"></em>\n                Eat fresh scallops and mussels harborside in picture&#8209;book&#8209;pretty Honfleur. \n    </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-le-havre-paris-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LEX', 'name': 'Leixões (Porto)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'leixoes-porto', 'desc_html': 'Porto is Portugal’s second city, and it\'s as colorful as it is memorable. Detail is key here, a place where the front doors are decorated with such a stunning variety of <em>azulejo</em> tiles that only by getting up close can you fully appreciate their intricacy. Explore on foot to unveil all the stunning scenery of Porto… like the Ribeira quarter, whose cobblestone-street scenery definitely falls a bit more on the "deliciously old-school" side. Be sure not to miss the city\'s port wine cellars — as you may have guessed, the city\'s most famous export took its name from the place itself.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-leixoes-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LGB', 'name': 'Long Beach (Los Angeles)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'long-beach-los-angeles', 'desc_html': 'When we talk about cruising from Los Angeles, fyi: we&rsquo;re talking about cruises from Long Beach. A short drive from LA is where you&rsquo;ll find this seaside Southern California city that&rsquo;s inseparable from its big-city neighbor, while undeniably moving to its own local beat. Dotted with dozens of parks, beaches and multiple public golf courses (fore times five!), Long Beach also boasts perhaps the world&rsquo;s most unique hotel &mdash; located aboard the old-time ocean liner The Queen Mary (which is haunted, or so go the rumors). You can experience it before one of Carnival&rsquo;s cruises from Long Beach, but definitely don&rsquo;t miss the glitzy, big-city Los Angeles &mdash; the right place to experience the left-coast life. Take in the storied sights of this City of Angels, from its modern museums and high-end shopping to its funky seaside towns and star-studded SoCal sights dotting the hills and boulevards. Hollywood &mdash; hooray! So if you&rsquo;re dreaming about a cruise from Los Angeles, remember: Carnival&rsquo;s cruises from Long Beach are just the ticket.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Climb aboard the <em>Queen Mary</em>, a glamorous 1930s ocean liner.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Find your favorite star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll through the art and antiquities of the Getty Center<sup style="font-size: 70%;">&reg;</sup>.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take the backlot tour of Universal Studios<sup style="font-size: 70%;">&trade;</sup> for a look at Hollywood mythmaking.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Gaze into the starry night sky through the Griffith Observatory\'s<sup style="font-size: 70%;">&reg;</sup> giant telescope.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-los-angeles-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LGN', 'name': 'La Goulette (Tunis)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'la-goulette-tunis', 'desc_html': ' Many of Tunisia\'s\xa0imports arrive at La Goulette, and so will you!\xa0Once a popular Tunisian vacation destination, La Goulette\'s\xa0seaside vibe earned it the nickname "Little Sicily." Today the historic kasbah shouldn\'t be overlooked, and the beaches are still beautiful, but La Goulette is also your gateway to Tunis, Tunisia\'s can\'t-miss capital and largest city. A metropolis of nearly three million, Tunis features many sights and sounds\xa0that haven\'t changed much in ages, and Jamaa ez-Zitouna in the Old Town might just be Exhibit A. This street is home to traditional street markets, or souks, full of small stalls offering handmade products. The narrow streets of the old-town Medina section hold more cultural and historical treasures — mosques, palaces and such — to discover. But another option for spending your time would be exploring the Roman ruins of Carthage, and over in that direction is also Sidi Bou Said, perhaps the opposite. This literal city on a hill — well, it\'s really more of a town — is the very picture of seaside Mediterranean perfection, with whitewashed walls and blue accents under the sun.\n', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-la-goulette-tunis-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LIH', 'name': 'Nawiliwili, Kauai', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'nawiliwili', 'desc_html': 'Photos of Kauai need no filter &mdash; nature&rsquo;s got amazing palettes all ready for you. Hawaii&rsquo;s oldest, greenest, and most dramatic island, Kauai offers visitors a chance to explore rainforests and play in the surf. On your Carnival cruise to Kauai, Hawaii, get a helicopter&rsquo;s-eye view of the inaccessible parts of the island&hellip; or get up close with a tour of Waimea Canyon or the Na Pali Coast. (Or just relax on the island&rsquo;s incredible beaches on your Kauai cruise.)<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take in the beauty of the 3,000-ft. deep Waimea Canyon.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit thundering waterfalls and remote beaches with a tour of the Na Pali Coast.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy Kauai&rsquo;s ocean playground at the numerous beaches circling the island.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-hawaii-itinerary-kauai-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LIS', 'name': 'Lisbon', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'lisbon', 'desc_html': 'Discover Portugal&rsquo;s bright, fun-loving capital city on your cruise to Lisbon. Straddling seven hills, hugging the banks of the River Tagus &mdash; and crowned by the storybook castle of S&atilde;o Jorge &mdash; Lisbon, Portugal is a visually stunning place to visit, and arriving by sea is doing it right! The nation&rsquo;s hundreds of years of nautical heritage is concentrated in Lisbon, and the riverside Bel&eacute;m district is where Portuguese navigators like Magellan and Vasco da Gama would begin their journeys. Today, cruise ship passengers make landfall not far from that spot. By the way, the city has modern claims to fame, too! With its rumbling yellow trams and stately plazas, irresistible patisseries and bluesy fado music, expect exotic sights and sounds &mdash; and more &mdash; on your cruise to Lisbon.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Be captivated by the skyline views from Lisbon&rsquo;s Castelo de S&atilde;o Jorge.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the Belem Tower fortress, built in the 16th century to defend the harbor.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore the Jer&oacute;nimos Monastery, which was designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1983.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-lisbon-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LMO', 'name': 'Limón', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'limon', 'desc_html': 'Cruise to Costa Rica to discover why the locals have been called the happiest people in the world. Costa Rica&rsquo;s abundant ecotourism treasures await when you board your Carnival cruise to Lim&oacute;n. From here you can soar above rainforests, feel the mist from tumbling waterfalls, and swim in clear Caribbean seas. These make Lim&oacute;n, Costa Rica a top spot in the region for embarking on eco-adventures. When you cruise to Lim&oacute;n, don&rsquo;t forget to check out the city itself, the source for millions of bananas that get shipped northward every year. Whether in the Caribbean waters or amongst nature on land, you&rsquo;ll feel refreshed and invigorated by your cruise to Costa Rica.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Raft the dam-controlled Reventaz&oacute;n River&rsquo;s powerful rapids.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Zipline through the canopy of the rainforest.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Spread out on the golden sands of a spectacular Caribbean beach.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore the Veragua Rainforest, located on the hills overlooking the Port of Lim&oacute;n.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-limon-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LOD', 'name': 'Dover (London)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'dover-london', 'desc_html': 'Be captivated by cliff-top walks and 2,000 years of history on cruises from Dover, England. Set against the backdrop of the White Cliffs and peering across to France on the other side of the English Channel, Dover&rsquo;s setting is a sight to behold. This bustling English port is steeped in history and coastal beauty. Explore the secret tunnels beneath medieval Dover Castle and easily make your way to iconic London landmarks like Buckingham Palace and the House of Parliament.<ul class="features-list">\n\t<li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tFollow in King Henry II&rsquo;s footsteps at Dover Castle.\n\t</li>\n    <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tFeel the power of the sea as you hike along the White Cliffs of Dover.\n\t</li>\n    <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tImmerse yourself in the City of Canterbury, literary setting of Chaucer&rsquo;s epic tales.\n\t</li>\n    <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tCatch the changing of the guard at Buckingham Palace.\n\t</li>\n  <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tSnap a selfie in front of Big Ben, London&rsquo;s celebrity clock tower.\n\t</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itinerary-london-dover-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LOM', 'name': 'Lembar (Lombok)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'lembar-lombok', 'desc_html': '<p>A Carnival cruise to Lembar (Lombok) is the perfect chance to get away from it all and create memories that will last forever. A Lombok cruise reveals an island that features stunning mountains, green pastures and tall trees as far as the eye can see.</p>\n    <p>Spend time walking along pristine Senggigi Beach and make the most of the spectacular location. Lose yourself in the Lingsar temple and appreciate the rich cultural traditions of the area.</p>\n    <p>A Lombok cruise is also about more than the destination. With more than 45 activities onboard, the fun and adventure will never stop.</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Stroll along white sandy beaches.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Find harmony at the Lingsar temple.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Witness amazing marine life.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Make the most of a Lombok cruise.\n    </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/AU/Lombok_Tropical-Bay_v1-1920x1080-jpg.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LPL', 'name': 'Liverpool', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'liverpool', 'desc_html': "Liverpool, England has a proud 800 years of history behind it, with a rich and varied cultural scene, even if you — somehow! — ignore what happened there 60-ish years ago. Yes, this is where the biggest rock band of all time got their start, and the city where you’ll still find the actual Penny Lane and Strawberry Field. But before the lads and their contemporaries made the local “Merseybeat” sound world-famous, Liverpool was already home to Europe’s original communities of Black and Chinese folks, the UK’s longest-running symphony, World Heritage Site Royal Albert Dock… not to mention a pair of ancient cathedrals that includes the UK’s largest. Venture elsewhere in the Liverpool Bay region and you’ll find sights like the glacier-formed Windermere Lake (England's longest), the meticulously-preserved city of Chester with its ancient walls, plus the first King Edward’s Conwy Castle, straight out of the 1280s.", 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-liverpool-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LVI', 'name': 'Le Verdon (Bordeaux)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'le-verdon-bordeaux', 'desc_html': 'There are many ways to get to Bordeaux, France’s wine country that since Roman times has been best known for its unique blends of reds. Le Verdon is a great way, but all that said, it’s more than just a gateway to Bordeaux, but a destination all its own. Known locally as Le Verdon-sur-Mer, this spot combines scenic beach and lighthouse views, while the river gorge area naturally lends itself to options for active fun like biking and hiking. But you really don’t want to miss Bordeaux, which goes beyond its iconic wines with neoclassical architecture, incredible parkland and even the largest city square in Western Europe.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-bordeaux-le-verdon-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LVO', 'name': 'Livorno (Florence & Pisa)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'livorno-florence-pisa', 'desc_html': 'Livorno is the coastal gateway to beautiful Tuscany, where you&rsquo;ll find both fan-favorite Pisa and Florence, the cradle of the Renaissance. Florence houses some of the world\'s greatest works of art, from masters like Leonardo da Vinci and Boticelli, plus Michelangelo\'s David and the Duomo, whose terrace offers breathtaking views of the city&rsquo;s red-tiled roofs and narrow medieval lanes. Then there&rsquo;s Pisa, Florence&rsquo;s rival for political power and a brash, commercial seafaring town that once rivaled the great maritime powers Venice and Genoa. Of course you&rsquo;ll visit the Leaning Tower, but don&rsquo;t stop there. Palazzo Agostini houses 12th century remains of Pisa&rsquo;s city walls, and Piazza dei Cavalieri was consistently the center of Pisan history.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Fall in love with Renaissance art at the Uffizi on your Florence cruise.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Gaze into goldsmiths&rsquo; glittering cases along the famous Ponte Vecchio.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-livorno-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'MAN', 'name': 'Manzanillo', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'manzanillo', 'desc_html': 'Drop anchor in Mexico&rsquo;s biggest commercial port on Carnival cruises to Manzanillo. Don&rsquo;t let the business bustle of this Pacific coast city fool you &mdash; Manzanillo, Mexico is a classic seaside resort at heart. With a pair of gently curving bays, Manzanillo is flush with long golden beaches for snorkeling, swimming and siestas. Battle magnificent sailfish in Mexico&rsquo;s fishing capital, or scuba dive with eagle rays when you cruise to Manzanillo.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Claim a patch of sand as your own on Playa Las Brisas.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Spot snow-capped volcanoes rising above Comala.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Hook silvery sailfish on a fishing excursion on your cruise to Manzanillo.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-mexico-itinerary-manzanillo-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'MCZ', 'name': 'Maceio', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'maceio', 'desc_html': 'You could call Maceió a beachy tourist destination… and that\'s honestly not a bad thing at all, when you consider the variety available here: warm seas, coastal resorts and beaches galore, which even get the locals flocking over this way to enjoy a little sand and sun. There\'s plenty of "praia" to choose from, like Praia Pajuçara and its coral reef, Praia do Francês with its dense thicket of palm trees, and Praia de Ponta Verde, located off the city center, featuring a huge chair photo-op and just plain sand and sun. (Praia means "beach," by the way — though you probably guessed!', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-south-america-itinerary-maceio-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'MEC', 'name': 'Manta', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'manta', 'desc_html': "Manta has been a crossroads of civilizations for longer than many cities and countries have existed. The seaport dates back to the times of the Incas, and doubtlessly helped fueled the growth of the settlement into a city of 200,000. With population has come modern comforts like restaurants and nightlife, but Manta has so many of its charming qualities of yesteryear. You can still find artisans handmaking wicker items at the village of Montecristi — and even Panama hats. (Despite the name, this is where they originated!) Manta's archaeological museum is ready to show you visions of\xa0the past, particularly ceramics of the Manteño-Huancavilca culture, some dating back over 1,000 years. Natural beauty is timeless, and the Pacoche Wildlife Refuge is a prime example, home to howler monkeys, among other plants and creatures.\xa0", 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-south-america-itinerary-manta-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'MIA', 'name': 'Miami', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'miami', 'desc_html': '<p>Dreaming of an island vacation? Make your dreams a reality with one of Carnival&rsquo;s year-round cruises from Miami.&nbsp;Because it&rsquo;s so close to the Caribbean and The Bahamas, Miami is known as the cruise capital of the world. But it&rsquo;s more than just convenient &mdash; rev up for your cruise from Miami with the city&rsquo;s nonstop action, from party-ready South Beach to the Mediterranean style of Coral Gables, plus spicy Little Havana, which hums to an island beat. Once you&rsquo;ve experienced all the South Florida architectural beauty, energetic street life and sun-kissed beaches, you may want to extend your stay in the Magic City after your cruise returns.</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Drink up the sizzling nightlife on boisterous Ocean Drive.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See the classic architecture in the South Beach Art Deco historic district.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Grab a cafecito and a Cubano sandwich on Calle Ocho in Little Havana.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy sightseeing, shopping, beaches, restaurants and bars on a hop-on/hop-off bus.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Glide past gators on an airboat ride in the Everglades.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-miami-2.jpg'},
    {'code': 'MOB', 'name': 'Mobile', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'mobile', 'desc_html': 'Mobile has been charming visitors since 1702, and today is a colorful, fun-loving city. It&#x2019;s one of the oldest port cities in America, and just blocks from the Mobile Cruise Terminal is a vibrant, walkable downtown district undergoing a serious renaissance. Check out the restaurants, bars, breweries, caf&#xE9;s, galleries and shops &#x2014; most locally owned &#x2014; and meet the folks who run these businesses for a warm, Southern-hospitality welcome.<ul class="features-list">\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>The Mobile/Tensaw Delta is just minutes from the cruise terminal and offers kayak, canoe and sightseeing tours before you set sail.</li>\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy traditional and contemporary takes on the fresh seafood and coastal cuisine that’s been spicing up Mobile’s restaurant scene.</li>\r\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-mobile-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'MRS', 'name': 'Marseille (Provence)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'marseilles-provence', 'desc_html': 'Marseille is France&rsquo;s second largest city, its largest port on the Mediterranean and &mdash; thanks in large part to Algerian immigration in the 1950s &mdash; a melting pot of people and cultures. Marseille&rsquo;s also a place of striking contrasts: at the picturesque Vieux Port, not far from the iconic fishing boats are sleek pleasure craft. Dominating the harbor is the infamous Chateau d&rsquo;If, the rocky prison from which Dumas&rsquo; Count of Monte Cristo escaped. Marseille is also your gateway to Provence. Explore the countryside around Arles and Avignon, as immortalized by Van Gogh, Cezanne, Matisse and Picasso.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Climb to Basilique Notre-Dame-de-la-Garde for a panoramic vista of the city and sea. </li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the world famous &ldquo;Calanques,&rdquo; listed as Natural heritage by UNESCO.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Admire the striped marble fa&ccedil;ade of the Cath&eacute;drale de la Major.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-marseille-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'MSY', 'name': 'New Orleans', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'new-orleans', 'desc_html': '<p>A Carnival cruise from New Orleans is your chance to discover the unmistakable charm and flavor of the Crescent City. Before or after you cruise, take a little time to explore the French Quarter &mdash;&nbsp;romantic as ever, with restaurants serving up heaping helpings of savory Creole cuisine, and nightclubs and street musicians playing the kind of jazz that gets your toes tapping. The best part is, you can soak up some of this flavor before sailing on one of our cruises out of New Orleans. &nbsp;Whether you&rsquo;re whooping it up on Bourbon Street, listening to the Jackson Square trumpeters, or hearing the ghosts whisper at eerie St. Louis Cemetery No. 1, spending extra time in the Big Easy is a must when cruising from New Orleans. Time your NOLA cruise right, and you can step out with the parades of Jazz Fest and Mardi Gras.</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Eat, drink, and revel in the lively French Quarter.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Spot mansions peeking out from lush greenery in the Garden District.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Dunk sugary beignets in your <em>caf&eacute; au lait</em> at Caf&eacute; du Monde.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Celebrate the history of Mardi Gras before you cruise from New Orleans.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-new-orleans-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'MTB', 'name': 'Montego Bay', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'montego-bay', 'desc_html': 'When it comes to cruises to Jamaica, this is a port you won&rsquo;t want to miss. Prepare to let your hair down and kick back to seductive reggae rhythms on your cruise to Montego Bay. Boasting some of Jamaica&rsquo;s finest beaches, shopping, restaurants and golf courses, &ldquo;Mo Bay&rdquo; (as it&rsquo;s affectionately known) is a tropical live-wire. Are you ready to immerse yourself in the town&rsquo;s festive energy? Carnival&rsquo;s cruises to Montego Bay let you shop, swim, and play in Mo Bay to your heart&rsquo;s content &mdash; and sample Jamaica&rsquo;s rich culture on excursions into the island&rsquo;s breathtaking countryside. History lovers can experience the grandeur of old-time mansions and golfers can test their skills on a course with a Caribbean backdrop. Whatever you&rsquo;re into, we&rsquo;ve got everybody covered on our cruises to Montego Bay.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Lounge on the golden sands of a palm-shaded beach.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour the grand interior of a haunted mansion.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Test your skills and perfect your putting on a seaside golf course.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Swing to reggae sounds at a barefoot beach bar when you cruise to Jamaica.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-montego-bay-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'MTK', 'name': 'Martinique', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'martinique', 'desc_html': 'You might guess from the name that Martinique has a little French in it. But you might be surprised to learn that this far-flung island is more than just a Francophile &mdash; it&rsquo;s technically part of France. Pretty cool for a southern Caribbean gem, oui? The food consists not only of the French influences, but a hearty helping of the local staples like seafood and tropical fruits and vegetables. The big can&rsquo;t-miss is a curry called &ldquo;colombo,&rdquo; the peak of local cuisine. The island&rsquo;s actual peak comes in the form of Mont Pel&eacute;e, standing 4,500 feet above sea level. There&rsquo;s variety on this island, from forests to savannas to beaches. Speaking of beaches, you&rsquo;ll find white-sand beaches on Martinique&rsquo;s south end, with black-sand beaches to the north.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the Clement House Plantation &mdash; one of the most famous plantation homes in the Caribbean &mdash; and see the historic house, gardens, sugar cane and banana fields.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Check out Balata Gardens near Fort de France. See over 3,000 varieties of tropical plants from around the world.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>The adventurous can hike into the primeval splendor of Martinique\'s tropical rainforest.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-martinique-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'MYK', 'name': 'Mykonos', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'mykonos', 'desc_html': 'How’d you get so perfect, Mykonos? Check out some pics of the town and you might wonder why the buildings are so perfectly white. Or maybe you won’t wonder, since it’s easy to just get lost in awe of the island’s picturesque beauty, of how perfect it all just happens to be, from the Cycladic architecture with brilliant blue accents to the stoic windmills. Just why Mykonos became one of Greece’s most iconic international travel destinations, a nightlife capital for the rich in the ’60s and ’70s — and today continues to attract seekers of great shopping, dining and strolling — all becomes evident when you visit. Also, don’t miss Mykonos’s neighboring island, Delos, for another side of Greece, the side with archaeological ruins of temples and sanctuaries from ancient times.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-mykonos-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'MZT', 'name': 'Mazatlán', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'mazatlan', 'desc_html': 'Go from the opera house to the lighthouse with Carnival cruises to Mazatl&aacute;n, Mexico. This city&rsquo;s 17-mile-long beach has rolling swells for surfers and calm waters for swimmers. Thatch-roofed shacks serve the freshest seafood and beach bars pour crisp cervezas with lime. On cruises to Mazatl&aacute;n, don\'t forget to head out beyond the bustling beach scene to experience the charming colonial core of Viejo Mazatl&aacute;n, complete with ornate churches and photogenic Spanish mansions.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>\nTry the chill life on for size on the photogenic Deer Island.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Sip an ice-cold Pac&iacute;fico beer &mdash; Maztal&aacute;n&rsquo;s original brew &mdash; on Playa S&aacute;balo.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the colonial villages of Copala and Concordia on your Mazatl&aacute;n cruise.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-mexico-itinerary-mazatlan-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'NAP', 'name': 'Naples (Amalfi/Pompeii)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'naples-amalfi-pompeii', 'desc_html': 'Not just one of Italy&rsquo;s oldest cities, but among the world&rsquo;s oldest, Naples and its surrounding area has over thousands of years contributed innovations to not only the culinary and visual arts, but the development of everything from language to music. Today, you\'ll feel the friendly spirit of this sunny metropolis as you sample its historic sights, fabulous shopping galleria and irresistible cuisine. But don&rsquo;t limit yourself to the city itself &mdash; Mount Vesuvius, the spectacular Amalfi Coast, and the romantic isle of Capri\'s famous Blue Grotto are all just a short distance away. The well-known, buried city of Pompeii is an archeological wonder, and not far from Naples.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See treasures adorning the Duomo&rsquo;s chapel, including silver statues of San Gennaro.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Step back to life from Roman times in Pompeii.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Peek inside Queen Maria Amalia&rsquo;s boudoir at the Museo Nazionale de Capodimonte.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-naples-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'NAS', 'name': 'Nassau', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'nassau', 'desc_html': '<p>Sightseeing, swimming and soaking up the island flavor &mdash; it\'s all yours for the taking on a Carnival cruise to Nassau, Bahamas.&nbsp;Boasting balmy breezes and jumping to a bouncy calypso beat, Nassau promises sizzling fun in the sun. The historic and cultural heart of The Bahamas is one of the world&rsquo;s most popular cruise destinations &mdash; one million travelers board cruises to Nassau every year. Carnival guests come for fine beaches, shopping, water sports, and fun-filled attractions at the Atlantis Resort, connected to Nassau by a bridge to Paradise Island. Throw in a chance to swim with dolphins, or do a little slipping and sliding at a water park, and it\'s clear what makes Nassau a top spot for cruisers of all ages.&nbsp;</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop the straw market for cute and kitschy crafts.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Pose for the classic &lsquo;dolphin kiss&rsquo; during a private island swim with the dolphins.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Relax on the white sands of a private island.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll 18th-century colonial streets and climb the sandstone Queen&rsquo;s Staircase.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-bahamas-itinerary-nassau-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'NYC', 'name': 'Manhattan, New York City', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'manhattan-new-york-city', 'desc_html': 'Start your Carnival cruise from the city that defined \'cosmopolitan\': New York City. This urban island overflows with art and architecture, lively ethnic neighborhoods, designer shops... and the best restaurants in the world, from the ultra-high-end to the comfy neighborhood hole-in-the-wall. The top sights are clustered in Midtown Manhattan &mdash; you can easily check out Grand Central Terminal, shop on Fifth Avenue, and see the twinkling lights of Broadway<sup style="font-size: 70%;">&reg;</sup> in Times Square on the same day. As your cruise leaving from New York glides down the Hudson River towards sunny islands or historic New England harbors, you\'ll pass metropolitan must-sees, world-renowned icons like the Empire State Building and the Statue of Liberty.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Pause amid the rush of Grand Central Terminal to look up at the starry ceiling.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Relax on the green lawns of Central Park.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Walk the mile-long Brooklyn Bridge before you cruise from New York.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Ascend the Empire State Building for 80-mile vistas.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-new-york-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'NYN', 'name': 'Nynäshamn (Stockholm)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'nynashamn-stockholm', 'desc_html': 'Located about 45 minutes from the quaint port town of Nynäshamn, where cruise ships dock, Sweden’s famous Stockholm was founded on Stadsholmen, a Swedish island. Oh, and it’s still there — but if you check a map you’ll see there’s a bit more Stockholm to go around these days. The city has actually expanded outward, now covering a very impressive (checking our map…) 14 <em>islands</em>! But great stats are just the beginning of what’s cool about Stockholm. This unique geography is predictably perfect for bridge lovers and canal explorers alike, while over on solid ground you’ll find equally cool sights to take in. Some options? Museums, palaces and old-town architecture made up of a delightful smörgåsbord of towers, cathedrals and copper-roofed buildings of all kinds. Plus there’s parkland galore, which accounts for a full 30% of Stockholm’s square meterage.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-stockholm-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'OAU', 'name': 'Otaru (Sapporo)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'otaru-sapporo', 'desc_html': 'Herring fishing! Coal mining! And would you believe… even music box manufacturing? Otaru, located on the island of Hokkaido, has certainly had a history of boom cycles, but the herring era, when its waters supplied all of Asia, holds an important place in the city’s history. After all, icons remain in the form of 19th century tycoons’ “herring mansions” — like the coast-hugging Otaru-shi Nishin Goden — which still draw the fascination of visitors. But even outside of history itself, the island’s scenic natural attractions, like national parks and its rugged west coast, have a timeless appeal. The freshness of the sushi is of course unsurprising, while the local whiskey distillery — perhaps surprisingly — uses traditional Scottish methods to produce a smoky malt. Don’t miss exploring the capital city, nearby Sapporo, and its spots for taking in the best sights, like Hitsujigaoka Observation Hill at Hokkaido Agricultural Experimental Station, which shows off the pastureland of Sapporo’s outskirts, and also the 482-foot Sapporo TV Tower at Sapporo Odori Park, which shares with the curious visitor some amazing city views, day and night.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-transpacific-port-otaru-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'OCJ', 'name': 'Ocho Rios', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'ocho-rios', 'desc_html': 'When it comes to dream vacations, an Ocho Rios cruise has to be near the top of the list. Nestled in an emerald Jamaican landscape, Ocho Rios is this island nation&rsquo;s prime cruise destination. Your cruise to Ocho Rios docks near some of the Caribbean&rsquo;s most fabled resorts and the cascading waterfalls of Dunn&rsquo;s River. Enjoy the best of Jamaica on your Carnival cruise to Ocho Rios, whether you&rsquo;re riding through lush sugarcane fields or touring the waterfront home where a legendary English novelist penned his early secret agent thrillers. From the reggae rhythm to the action-packed activities at Dunn&rsquo;s River Falls, an Ocho Rios, Jamaica, cruise has all the elements of a blockbuster film &mdash; one where you&rsquo;re the star. Start planning your Caribbean cruise with a call at Ocho Rios today and get ready for your close-up.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Climb a 600-ft. waterfall at Dunn&rsquo;s River Falls.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Get behind the wheel of a dune buggy and ride through the tropical Jamaican woodlands.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Chill out on a half-moon stretch of sugary sand.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Venture in search of the birthplace of reggae and the spirit of Bob Marley.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-ocho-rios-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'OGG', 'name': 'Kahului, Maui', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'kahului', 'desc_html': 'Millions of visitors from around the globe clamor to get to the magical isle of Maui, Hawaii, every year&hellip; and why they do is as clear as the water. Your Maui cruise brings you to this island of scenic beaches, thundering waterfalls, serene rainforests&hellip; plus breathtaking vistas, from the soaring peak of the dormant Haleakala volcano to the coral-rich marine world down below. Ascend to the home of the Hawaiian gods, explore historic villages, and enjoy a romantic star-filled night on your cruise to Maui.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the home of the sun atop the 10,000-foot volcano Haleakala.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Plunge beneath the waves and snorkel with rainbow-colored fish on Maui cruises.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Walk the buzzing streets of Lahaina, an old whaling port.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-hawaii-itinerary-maui-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ORF', 'name': 'Norfolk', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'norfolk', 'desc_html': 'If you live in the Mid-Atlantic area, might we suggest one of our cruises from Norfolk? Set sail, as thousands of seafaring Americans have, when you book a Carnival cruise from the 400-year-old seaport of Norfolk. The city is today the proud home of a sparkling waterfront filled with green parks, lively shopping malls, delicious restaurants&hellip; and even fascinating maritime museums and monuments. Before you cruise from Norfolk, you&rsquo;ll find yourself near two colonial villages &mdash; Colonial Williamsburg and Olde Towne Portsmouth &mdash; plus miles of beaches, and a blooming botanical garden. So definitely make time to explore before your cruise from Virginia, and round out your vacation with some history and picturesque sightseeing. Cruises from Norfolk also come with serious seafaring credentials &mdash; the city is home to one of the best maritime academies in the country.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Watch artisans blow glass at the Chrysler Museum of Art.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take a ferry to colonial Olde Towne Portsmouth village.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour the Norfolk waterfront by boat from the NAUTICUS museum.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Search for antique jewelry and furniture in the Ghent neighborhood.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-norfolk-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'OSA', 'name': 'Osaka (Kyoto)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'osaka-kyoto', 'desc_html': 'Japan’s second-largest city, Osaka, is the unofficial culinary capital of Japan. Its backstreets and laneways are full of restaurants and bars serving delicious local cuisine. Osaka is also home to some of the most famous castles, temples, and monuments from Japan’s past, just begging to be explored. The 16th-century Osaka Castle is a magnificent white and gold landmark not to be missed. First built in 728 the world heritage listed Todaiji Temple features the immense Great Buddha Statue and Sika deer that wander freely throughout the temple grounds.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour the world heritage listed Todaiji Temple</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stand in awe in front of Osaka Castle</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore all the shopping and entertainment of the Dotombori district</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit Kinkakuji Temple</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/AU/Kyoto_Kiyomizu-dera-Autumn-Sunset_v1-1920x1080-jpg.jpg'},
    {'code': 'PCL', 'name': 'Panama Canal Transit', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'panama-canal-transit', 'desc_html': 'Zoom your map way out and Panama looks like a small sliver of land, so a trip through its famous canal is a quickie, right? But not so fast — traversing the Panama Canal actually takes at least 20 hours! Cruise it and enjoy a zoomed-in real-life look at perhaps last century’s greatest engineering achievement… along with its surrounding lush, verdant lands. This testament to human audacity joins the Pacific and Caribbean in the most direct way possible, and is worth making a leisurely part of your vacation.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-panama-canal-itinerary-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'PCS', 'name': 'Princess Cays', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'princess-cays', 'desc_html': '<p>Cruise to Princess Cays and you&rsquo;ll come ashore in Love Boat Marina &mdash; a sign that this private resort on the island of Eleuthera, Bahamas was designed to be classic cruising perfection. Make landfall and discover an island&rsquo;s worth of vacation fun and amenities. You&rsquo;ll find a BBQ pit already fired up for lunch, and a supervised kids&rsquo; area ready to receive the little ones. Somewhere among the palm trees you might spy the exclusive adult-only retreat. By now it&rsquo;s clear that Princess Cays is good for more than just a beach day, but plan on fitting one in anyway &mdash; this wouldn&rsquo;t be a prime cruise destination without great things to do, and great ways to get wet, like swimming, kayaking and sailing.</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Rent a private beach bungalow and enjoy your stay in air-conditioned comfort.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Browse the shops for authentic, handmade Bahamian crafts.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour Princess Cays by dune buggy and sailboat to get the best views from all angles.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-bahamas-itinerary-princess-cays-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'PCV', 'name': 'Port Canaveral (Orlando)', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'port-canaveral-orlando', 'desc_html': 'Buckle up for big adventure on the Space Coast when you book a Carnival cruise from Port Canaveral, Florida. Fun in the sun is a mission easily accomplished in Port Canaveral: before or after your cruise, take time to blast off from the Kennedy Space Center, hug the turns in a stock car at the world famous speedway, and zoom through the screaming roller coasters of Orlando\'s theme parks. In addition to all these man-made thrills, cruises from Port Canaveral depart from a coastline of sugary sand beaches and protected islands for native wildlife.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See a rocket up close at the Kennedy Space Center<sup style="font-size: 70%;">&trade;</sup>.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Walk the bustling Cocoa Beach boardwalk before your cruise from Port Canaveral.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Encounter exotic animals and exciting adventures at Disney\'s Animal Kingdom<sup style="font-size: 70%;">&reg;</sup> park.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy an exciting wildlife and alligator tour by airboat.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-port-canaveral-3.jpg'},
    {'code': 'PDL', 'name': 'Ponta Delgada', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'ponta-delgada', 'desc_html': 'The Azores are breathtaking, and Ponta Delgada is the capital of breathtaking. These are facts. Experience the natural wonders of a remote Atlantic Ocean outpost on a Carnival cruise to Azores. S&atilde;o Miguel Island is your port for Azores cruises, where you can walk the rim of an extinct volcano crater, dine on cuisine cooked in volcanic water, and marvel at buildings decked in volcanic rock. The natural spectacle continues in the waters surrounding Azores, Portugal, home to breaching whales, jumping dolphins, swimming sea turtles.<ul class="features-list">\r\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See where it all started — Ribeira Grande is the island’s original town, and located atop a volcanic plateau.</li>\r\n <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Get a feel for the Furnas Valley, steamy home to hot springs, mud pools and geysers.</li>\r\n <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour a pineapple plantation and see how this island’s famous fruit is grown.</li>\r\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-ponta-delgada-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'PGR', 'name': 'Progreso, Yucatán', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'progreso', 'desc_html': 'Cruise to the Yucatán Peninsula for an unbeatable combination of breathtaking beaches and fascinating history. Carnival cruises to Progreso dock on Mexico’s Emerald Coast alongside the gulf, where hot pink flamingos gather by the hundreds and sun-bleached Maya pyramids rise from the jungle. This explosion of color and cultural landmarks is yours to explore on your cruise to Yucatán. Inland from Progreso’s golden beaches are the spectacular Maya ruins of Uxmal and the colorful city of Mérida, the region’s best shopping stop for handmade crafts. Discover the Maya world’s natural beauty and ancient history with cruises to Progreso, Mexico.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll through the Spanish colonial city of M&eacute;rida.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour Chichen Itza, one of the 7 wonders of the world.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore the Maya ruins at &mdash; ready for these? &mdash; Xcamb&oacute; and Dzibilchalt&uacute;n.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-mexico-itinerary-progreso-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'PHM', 'name': 'Phu My (Ho Chi Minh)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'phu-my-ho-chi-minh', 'desc_html': 'Beautiful beaches. Lively cities. Fascinating culture. Food that sends your tastebuds to the stars and back. Prepare to be pleasantly surprised when you visit vibrant Vietnam. The port of Phu My (pronounced "Foo Me") is your gateway to Ho Chi Minh City and the seaside resort of Vung Tau.\n\nA bustling city on the Mekong River, Ho Chi Minh City offers markets galore and, historical sites. The air is filled with the cries of street hawkers and honking horns. Bicycles, motorbikes and automobiles fly down the boulevards at dizzying speeds. And everywhere, friendly faces and warm greetings meet you.\n\n\n\n<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore vibrant markets\n</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take a cruise on the Mekong River\n</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the historic Cu Chi Tunnels\n</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-transpacific-itinerary-ho-chi-minh-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'PMI', 'name': 'Palma de Mallorca', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'palma-de-mallorca', 'desc_html': 'The largest island off the coast of Spain, Mallorca has been inhabited for thousands of years. Palma is its capital, and in recent times it&rsquo;s become a tourist-friendly destination that&rsquo;s also favored by Spanish royalty. Everyone can enjoy its natural wonders, like golden-sand beaches, tall pine groves and towering cliffs&hellip; not to mention grand churches, top-notch art museums, and lively plazas. The landscape is as varied as the northern mountains and the southern flatlands, with their almond and olive groves. Must-sees on this island fit for royalty include city views from the Castell Belver, and the Cathedral of Santa Maria&rsquo;s reflection from the lake at Parc de la Mar.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Watch the world flow by, from Parc de la Mar.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Be awed by the immense fa&ccedil;ade &mdash; not to mention the interior &mdash; of La Seu cathedral.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Taste some of the finest wines in the Island at Santa Catarina Winery.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-palma-de-mallorca-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'PMO', 'name': 'Palermo, Sicily', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'palermo-sicily', 'desc_html': 'Palermo is a cultural feast, a fascinating combination of East and West that is unlike any other European city on the Mediterranean. A simple stroll can serve to illustrate Palermo\'s rich heritage. The Quattro Canti is the great square at the heart of the city. A short walk past its 17th-century palazzos and fountains brings the traveler to the Palazzo dei Normanni, where elaborate tile work and mosaics showcase Islamic and Byzantine influences. The city abounds in such colorful sights, from the neo-classical Teatro Massimo &mdash; one of the largest opera houses in Europe &mdash; to the catacombs beneath the Capuchin convent, where thousands of mummified bodies lie in eternal rest.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Venture beyond Palermo (but don’t miss Palermo!) to Monreale’s Duomo, an artfully adorned cathedral.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Scope some of over 600 types of trees (and 30 types of birds) at the postcard-perfect Zingaro Natural Reserve.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Look up at the 19th-century Teatro Politeama, whose dramatic rooftop sculptures practically put on a show of their own.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-palermo-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'POS', 'name': 'Port of Spain', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'port-of-spain', 'desc_html': 'Trinidad’s the kind of place where different cultures mix in a way you can actually feel — in the food, the music, and the everyday buzz of the streets. In Port of Spain, Independence Square puts you right in the middle of the city’s energy, with historic gems like the Cathedral of the Immaculate Conception just steps away. Then shift gears at Woodford Square or unwind in the wide-open greenery of Queen’s Park Savannah. Along the northern coast, you’re surrounded by lush green hills that rise high above the island. The highest peaks — El Cerro del Aripo and El Tucuche — tower more than 900 meters above sea level, offering sweeping views. Not far away, you can explore winding mangroves in the Caroni wetlands, where vibrant birdlife — including the striking Scarlet Ibis — fills the landscape. It’s not flashy or overdone — just a place to slow down and explore at your own pace.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-port-of-spain.jpg'},
    {'code': 'PSO', 'name': 'Icy Strait Point', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'icy-strait-point', 'desc_html': 'Icy Strait Point is a sight, alright, for eyes that hunger for the greens of the dense Tongass Forest, the azure waters of Port Frederick, and the spot where these come together. Make landfall here and find yourself in Hoonah, where the native Huna Tlingit tribe have lived for thousands of years. Not quite as old &mdash; only about 100 years young &mdash; are remnants of the local cannery, a symbol of the industry that put this area on modern maps. Hugely important then but long out of operation, the cannery today is restored and tourable, just one historical signpost in a place as well-known for its natural sights.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Watch whales and try your eye at sighting a brown bear on the same excursion.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Breeze from the top of Hoonah Mountain to the beach of Icy Strait Point on a mile-plus zip-line ride.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Learn about the history and customs of the native Huna Tlingit tribe through interpretive song, dance and storytellings.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-alaska-itinerary-icy-strait-point-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'PVR', 'name': 'Puerto Vallarta', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'puerto-vallarta', 'desc_html': 'Whether you&rsquo;re seeking quality beach time or action-packed adventures, cruises to Puerto Vallarta will deliver the vacation you&rsquo;ve been craving. Reigning over Banderas Bay and bordered by the tropical forests of the Sierra Madre Mountains, Puerto Vallarta, is both a modern beach resort and an eco-adventure launching pad. On Mexico cruises to Puerto Vallarta, scuba dive with manta rays, spot dolphins playing in the waves, and hike to jungle cascades. Admire contemporary Latin American art in this breezy seaside city on your Carnival cruise to Puerto Vallarta.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Fly through the lush green forest canopy, secured to one zippy zip-line.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Pay homage to Ava Gardner and John Huston before snorkeling from Playa Mismaloya or Las Caletas &mdash; spots made famous by 1964&rsquo;s The Night of the Iguana.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Join a whale-watching tour in winter, when humpback whales cruise through Banderas.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-mexico-itinerary-puerto-vallarta-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'PWM', 'name': 'Portland', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'portland', 'desc_html': 'Walk Maine&rsquo;s largest city and follow in the footsteps of your fellow seafarers, past and present, on a Carnival cruise to Portland. Perched on green bluffs overlooking Casco Bay, Portland is a place where lobstermen still ply the briny Maine seas and wooden fishing boats chug through the harbor. Portland cruises pull into a modern-day seaport of sleek high-rises towering over a revitalized Old Port area, alive with brewpubs, restaurants, and shops.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Meander the colorful streets of Old Port, or see a slice of 19th-century life in the Victoria Mansion.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Get a panoramic view of Maine&rsquo;s craggy coast from the cliff-top Portland Head Lighthouse.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Learn why the other Portland (in Oregon) was named for this east coast original.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll the Eastern Promenade Pathway above bustling Casco Bay.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-new-england-itinerary-portland-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'QSR', 'name': 'Salerno (Amalfi/Pompeii)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'salerno-amalfi-pompeii', 'desc_html': 'Salerno is an Italian city that’s old to the tune of 2,000 years, and blends ancient and modern — not to mention a healthy dose of medieval — together in a package that features enough sights to definitely make Carnival cruises to Salerno worthwhile. Topping the ‘worth seeing’ list you’ll find Villa Comunale, a very, very green public garden located outside of the old city hall, and definitely don’t miss a waterside stroll along Lungomare Trieste during your cruise. If you’re looking to venture out of Salerno on this leg of your vacation — and you should — you’re not far at all from the culture-packed Naples, the incomparably beautiful Amalfi Coast and the buried historical city of Pompeii.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-port-itinerary-salerno-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'RIN', 'name': 'Ringaskiddy (Cork)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'ringaskiddy-cork', 'desc_html': 'Ringaskiddy is your jumping-off point for Cork, a city that’s always had a bit of a story behind it, even if today it’s more about energy, creativity, and good vibes than old tales. The River Lee splits the city into little islands, which makes wandering around feel like a mini urban adventure: bridges everywhere, new corners to explore, and plenty of spots to grab a great coffee or snap a photo. If you’re into historic icons, check out the spiky Gothic silhouette of St. Fin Barre’s Cathedral or the tower of St. Anne’s with its giant salmon weather vane—but they’re less “textbook history lesson” and more “wow, that looks cool” moments as you weave through the city. And then there’s the quick trip to Blarney Castle, where you can kiss the famous Blarney Stone, and see if you walk away with that little boost of charm it’s known for. Whether you believe the legend or not, it’s all part of the fun of exploring Cork from Ringaskiddy.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-ringaskiddy-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'RIO', 'name': 'Rio de Janeiro', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'rio-de-janeiro', 'desc_html': 'If you love the thought of turning some of the most legendary, coveted names in travel — think Copacabana, Ipanema, Corcovado — into destinations on your next vacation, it sounds to us like you\'re ready to Rio! From surfing to sunning to dancing, dancing and dancing some more, Rio de Janiero has more than a little of everything you\'re after. It also has one of the most iconic sculptures anywhere, ever — with arms open wide, the 125-foot Christ the Redeemer towers 2,400 feet above Corcovado Peak. But there\'s more to Rio than numbers — you can\'t quantify those sweet city and beach views you\'ll get from atop Sugarloaf Mountain (Pão de Açúcar), though it\'s well worth the cable car trip up. Exploring the world\'s biggest urban forest probably wasn\'t on your to-do list, but Tijuca National Park and its 8,000 acres and hundreds of species is ready to change that. Don\'t be surprised to find yourself humming "Cidade maravilhosa" — Rio\'s anthem — before this is all over!', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-south-america-itinerary-rio-de-janeiro-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'RTB', 'name': 'Isla Tropicale, Roatan', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'isla-tropicale', 'desc_html': '<style>\r\n  .trade_styling {\r\n    font-size: 70%;\r\n    position: relative;\r\n    top: -0.3em;\r\n  }\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nCruise to Isla Tropicale and discover Roatán\'s spectacular blend of nature, wildlife and island beauty. Home to 42 species of hummingbirds and surrounded by the world’s second-largest coral reef, this tropical paradise offers lush landscapes and vibrant marine life at every turn.\r\n<br /><br />\r\nWe’ve added to a destination you already love, Mahogany Bay, and made it better with more ways to enjoy your day. At the center of it all is the new Mangrove Bay Pool & Swim-Up Bar. Enjoy this brand‑new pool area and swim-up bar and experience all‑day fun in the sun. Wiggle your toes on the golden sand beaches, then take a dip in the aquamarine waters of the Caribbean. Grab a bite at a beachside restaurant or enjoy a refreshing tropical drink at a bar. \r\n<br /><br />\r\nAt Isla Tropicale, you’ll discover a place where Roatán’s natural beauty meets a vibrant island energy you won’t find anywhere else. From snorkeling and diving along the colorful reef to exploring pristine wildlife reserves and relaxing on the beach, Roatán is one of the Caribbean’s most unforgettable natural escapes. And whether you’re getting a bird’s-eye view of paradise on a scenic chairlift, discovering a nature trail with great photo opportunities or kayaking along the coastline, there are plenty of air, land and sea excursions for everyone.\r\n<br /><br />\r\nIsla Tropicale is part of the Paradise Collection<span class="trade_styling">&trade;</span> by Carnival, where each cruise destination showcases a different slice of paradise, from breathtaking, white sand beaches to vibrant cultures and unforgettable excursions.\r\n</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Swim in the sparkling aquamarine waters off West Bay</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy panoramic views on a scenic chairlift ride</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Dine on Honduran specialties in local West End restaurants</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Watch capuchin monkeys play in Gumbalimba Park</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-isla-tropicale-roatan-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SAI', 'name': 'San Antonio (Santiago)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'san-antonio-santiago', 'desc_html': "The port town of San Antonio, Chile, is your gateway to the capital … and Santiago de Chile, you could say, has it all. With sights ancient and modern, vibes elegant and festive, this city embodies the best of everything, and as a metropolis of over 5 million people, you could guess that it has quite a bit of it. Old and new share the stage in Santiago, with Palacio de la Real Audencia and the National Museum of History making the same must-visit list as the hip, artsy barrio Bellavista and\xa0barrio Italia neighborhoods.\xa0Nature is never far in Santiago, even in city views — imagine a neoclassical cathedral reflected in the glass of a nearby office tower, and the snow-capped Andes are usually there backdropping the sights. The beating heart of Chile's famous wine country can be found in local regions like Casablanca and Maipo Maipo Valley, contributing to the country's top-10 stature in the wine world. But while we're talking sippables, Chile's iconic pisco sour is the drink you simply shouldn't miss.", 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-south-america-itinerary-san-antonio-santiago-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SDH', 'name': 'Souda (Chania), Crete', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'souda-chania-crete', 'desc_html': 'You’ll dock in Souda, a working port just a few miles from Chania on Crete’s north coast. From there, it’s an easy ride into town — and that’s where things get interesting. Chania’s old Venetian Harbor is the heart of it all. A lighthouse stands at the edge, and the old stone shipyards still line the waterfront, reminders that this place has been building and defending ships for centuries. Greeks, Romans, Venetians, Ottomans — they all passed through, and you can see it in the buildings and narrow backstreets near the harbor. Wander the tight alleys, grab a coffee in the main square by the marble fountain, or pop into the Archaeological Museum for a look at artifacts that go way back. If ships are more your speed, the Maritime Museum’s worth a stop. Out by Souda Bay, you’ll find the old Aptera Fortress overlooking the water — solid stone, big views, and plenty of history. Or head for Falassarna Beach, where clear water and olive groves keep things simple.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-souda-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SEA', 'name': 'Seattle', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'seattle', 'desc_html': 'Cruises departing from Seattle are your ticket to some of the most breathtaking scenery on Earth &mdash; they&rsquo;ll take you straight to Alaska! But there is plenty to see before or after your cruise, too. Carnival cruises from Seattle dock at the gates of the &ldquo;Emerald City.&rdquo; Set on Puget Sound in the shadow of Mt. Rainer, Seattle&rsquo;s stunning waterfront can be found curving past skyscrapers, historic neighborhoods, important museums, and the lush, rolling parks that give the city its green nickname. One of the best parts of cruising from Seattle is the opportunity to explore the iconic city, famous for its hip coffee culture and musical tastemaking. From its burgeoning foodie scene to its cultural treasures, this sparkling Pacific Northwest jewel is yours for the taking when you book a cruise from Seattle, Washington.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Zip up the Space Needle for views over the city&rsquo;s skyscrapers.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Snack on fresh-baked treats at the Pike Place Market.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Fuel up on Seattle&rsquo;s famous coffee before boarding cruises from Seattle.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-alaska-itinerary-seattle-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SFO', 'name': 'San Francisco', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'san-francisco', 'desc_html': 'Seaports have always been important throughout history&hellip;  it&rsquo;s about more than just the cargo, but the import and export of ideas. You could say that a city&rsquo;s seaside status almost necessarily creates a crossroads of cultures. All that said, something sets San Francisco apart! Maybe it&rsquo;s the year-round comfy weather that makes people want to spend their time outdoors, or perhaps it’s the spectacular food culture, or the history, or the hills, or the architecture. But one thing can be proven: San Francisco is beautiful, arguably the most romantic and cosmopolitan city in the U.S., and all of these elements go into the mix of making it a place you want to be, whether you know it or not. From the world&rsquo;s most recognizable bridge, The Golden Gate, to the quirky, flower-lined Lombard Street&hellip; it&rsquo;s no surprise that in SF even a former prison island — you knew we&rsquo;re talking about Alcatraz, right? — ends up being an iconic destination.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Send yourself to Alcatraz — for a little bit — as you visit the island that housed not only the prison, but a bird sanctuary and the west coast’s first lighthouse.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Walk among the world’s tallest trees, between 500 and 700 years old, at Muir Woods National Monument.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Get some of the city’s best views of the skyline — plus, actually, sea lions — at Pier 39 near Fisherman’s Wharf.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit San Francisco’s amazing neighbors like the charming, arty Sausalito and the serene Napa Valley wine region.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-san-francisco-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SIN', 'name': 'Singapore', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'singapore', 'desc_html': 'Embark on an unforgettable journey to Singapore with a Carnival Cruise. Each cruise getaway begins or ends with the Singapore Harbour, a destination that every cruise lover should experience. The cruise showcases the elegance of Singapore, with highlights including the world-renowned Orchard Road, the awe-inspiring Marina Bay, and the tranquil Botanical Gardens. This Southeast Asia cruise package promises to leave you spellbound. But with Carnival Cruise Line, the journey is about more than just the destination. It\'s about immersing yourself in exciting onboard activities, savouring a variety of dining options, and diving into the thrilling adventures you\'ve always dreamed of on the best cruise ship. <br /><br />\n\nA Singapore cruise day rewards the hungry and the curious in equal measure. The Hawker Chan at Chinatown Complex (the world\'s most affordable Michelin star) is a fitting place to start your morning, before walking the blue-tiled Thian Hock Keng Temple and the spice-scented lanes of Ann Siang Hill. Architecture fans can cross to the Marina Bay waterfront for the full sweep of the skyline: the Helix Bridge, the ArtScience Museum and the gravity-defying SkyPark above it all. For nature in the middle of a city, the Singapore Botanic Gardens, a UNESCO World Heritage site, offers an hour of extraordinary calm just a short taxi ride from the cruise terminal. Cultural itineraries can extend through the Arab Quarter\'s Sultan Mosque, Kampong Glam\'s street art and the 24-hour food halls of Bugis.<br /><br />\n\nA Carnival Singapore cruise delivers one of Asia\'s most exhilarating cities on your own terms. No connecting flights, no hotel logistics, just a full day in a place that will leave you planning your return before you\'ve even got back to the ship. Browse our latest Singapore cruise itineraries and book your cruise to Singapore with Carnival today.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop on the famous Orchard Road.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Taste the spectacular dining options.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Marvel at Marina Bay Sands.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take in the famous Gardens by the Bay.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy everything a Singapore cruise offers.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-transpacific-singapore-port-3.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SIT', 'name': 'Sitka', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'sitka', 'desc_html': 'Sitka is where the Alaska Purchase happened&hellip; where the papers got signed and Alaska became part of the U.S. Sitka is not only historic, but huge &mdash; it&rsquo;s actually the largest city-county in the country, larger than NYC. Unlike New York, Sitka is low on population, but jam-packed with amazing views of snow-capped mountains, lush green forests and Sitka Bay, itself dotted with an array of tiny islands.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore the coast of the volcanic St. Lazaria Island, from the relative comfort of a speeding ocean raft.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Cast a line and try your hand at reeling in a local salmon or halibut.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Scope out some wildlife, like the Alaska brown bear or Sitka black-tail deer, on nearby Kruzof Island.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-alaska-port-sitka-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SJU', 'name': 'San Juan', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'san-juan', 'desc_html': 'Cruises from San Juan, Puerto Rico offer a magical blend of natural island charm and man-made wonders. Historic San Juan, once nothing more than cobblestone streets and the distinctive architecture of the Spanish who founded it, is now a modern world capital. And, as you&rsquo;ll see on Carnival&rsquo;s cruises from Puerto Rico, it&rsquo;s kept these classical features! Among the peaceful shaded courtyards and commanding colonial fortresses of El Morro and San Cristobal, urban explorers will find a cosmopolitan city of wide boulevards, lively caf&eacute;s, highly-regarded galleries and designer boutiques&hellip; not to mention gold-sand beaches and nearby rainforest jungles. San Juan, Puerto Rico is where the old world meets the new &mdash; and you can enjoy them both when you choose one of our cruises from San Juan.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Castillo San Felipe del Morro (a.k.a. &ldquo;El Morro&rdquo;) features amazing history and the best view of the San Juan harbor.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>The Bacardi distillery<sup style="font-size: 70%;">&reg;</sup> spans 127 acres of land, and over 100 years of history.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Vieques is an island\'s island &mdash; literally, featuring amazing beaches and found off the coast of Puerto Rico.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Munch on <em>mofongo</em>, a fried plantain delicacy, a staple of menus throughout San Juan.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-san-juan-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SKY', 'name': 'Skagway', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'skagway', 'desc_html': 'Walk in the footsteps of pioneers and profiteers on Carnival cruises to Skagway. Gold seekers stampeded to the Klondike more than 100 years ago and built Skagway, Alaska as their lawless outpost of brothels, saloons, and gambling dens. Today, the town is more of a time capsule from the past, with carefully preserved buildings and streets brimming with history. Live the final chapter of America&rsquo;s Wild West era on a Skagway cruise.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore the restored period buildings in Klondike Gold Rush National Historic District.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Board quaint, antique passenger cars for a breathtaking mountain train ride.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Follow the trail of the sourdoughs &mdash; prospectors who risked their lives climbing Chilkoot Pass.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Fly to awesome mountains by helicopter and experience the ice fields via dogsled.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-alaska-itinerary-skagway-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SLC', 'name': 'St. Lucia', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'st-lucia', 'desc_html': 'Take a walk through St. Lucia&rsquo;s landscapes of magenta bougainvillea tumbling from mossy peaks, and listen to birdsong filling the air. This is just a slice of island life that awaits  on cruises to St. Lucia. With some of the Caribbean&rsquo;s most dramatic scenery &mdash; from the velvety twin peaks of the Pitons to the shimmering white-sand beaches &mdash; independent St. Lucia speaks with a decidedly French lilt. Climb green-mantled mountains and snorkel in jade seas on your sun-filled Carnival cruise to St. Lucia.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the Sulphur Springs for a warm mud bath in a hot mineral pool at the bottom of the springs</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Spend a relaxing afternoon on the beaches of Pigeon Island.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop in the colorful Central Market of the capital city.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Enjoy a fun cruise along St. Lucia&rsquo;s coastline to experience the magnificent Pitons.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-st-lucia-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SPO', 'name': 'Seogwipo (Jeju)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'seogwipo-jeju', 'desc_html': 'Seogwipo is your gateway to beautiful Jeju Island. As soon as you step foot on Jeju it will be easy to see why it’s often referred to as “The Hawaii of Korea”. Soaring Mount Hallasan, a dormant volcano covered in lush green vegetation dominates the stunning landscape which also features white sandy beaches, crystal-clear waters and winding coastal trails. Visitors can hike up the mountain for breathtaking views of the crater lake near its summit or visit Cheonjeyeon Waterfall - known as the Pond of God. You can admire the falls from the Seonimgyo arch bridge, which offers a spectacular view of the surrounding rock formations and verdant parkland. Jeju\'s Jungmung Saekdal Beach is also popular, nestled in a secluded spot surrounded by cliffs. Alternatively, visitors can explore Seogwipo Healing Forest offering a serene 11 km-long forest trail through cypress and cedar trees.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Hike up Seongsan Ilchulbong (Sunrise Mountain)</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Cheonjeyeon waterfalls</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop local markets</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Sample local delicacies</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/AU/Seogwipo_Seongsan-Ilchulbong_v1-1920x1080-jpg.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SPU', 'name': 'Split', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'split', 'desc_html': 'A lot of port towns in the Mediterranean start off as a fishing village and grow to become something much more. Tale as old as time… but that’s <em>not</em> the backstory of Split, Croatia — Split has its roots in being the retirement home of a Roman emperor! Pretty lofty, and ages later you can still see why Diocletian himself settled here way back in the 4th century. The “old town” neighborhood is packed with history and charm, shopping and local flavor, cathedrals and the Temple of Jupiter… and museums help put it all in context. Some of nature’s best makes all the history seem surprisingly young, and it comes in the form of Krka National Park, home to natural limestone landscaping and some incredible waterfalls.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-split-croatia-port-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SRT', 'name': 'Santa Marta', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'santa-marta', 'desc_html': 'Santa Marta is the oldest city you&rsquo;ll find anywhere in Colombia &mdash; bragging rights for sure, but age isn&rsquo;t its only claim to fame. For one thing, it&rsquo;s located in a prime southern Caribbean spot upon Colombia&rsquo;s Costa Norte region. Costa Norte isn&rsquo;t just a beautiful place, but a cultural hub where Europeans, Afro-Colombians and indigenous people crossed paths, each bringing with them their own contributions to the local flavor.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Hike the lush vegetation of Tayrona National Park. You&rsquo;ll see animals, birds, plants, and even remnants of native Tayrona culture.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour the San Pedro de Alejandrino Villa and its manicured gardens, where Simon Bolivar spent his final days.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Walk along El Rodadero, a popular tourist destination with shops and modern hotels, built along the beautiful beaches.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-santa-marta-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'STK', 'name': 'St. Kitts', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'st-kitts', 'desc_html': 'Cruises to St. Kitts are a nature-lover&rsquo;s dream come true, and will wow anyone looking for a laidback Caribbean vacation full of postcard-ready scenery. Rainforests, waterfalls, and lovely crescents of sand aren&rsquo;t far from the ship on your Carnival cruise to St. Kitts. Cane fields climb the slopes of volcanic peaks, and the ruins of old mills and colonial plantation houses blanket the island. As you&rsquo;ll find on St. Kitts, there is plenty of action in the form of zip-lining and hiking but at heart, St. Kitts remains a sleepy and charming tropical community. Cruise to St. Kitts to bask in the Caribbean&rsquo;s sunny geniality and natural splendor.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Comb the grounds of a 17th-century British fort St. Charles, and its larger neighbor Brimstone Hill Fortress.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop for fresh mangos and guava fruit in the Circus Square marketplace.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Experience the adrenaline rush as you &ldquo;fly&rdquo; over the rainforest, 25 stories above the ground!</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stretch out on the beautiful white-sand beaches that surround the island.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-st-kitts-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'STT', 'name': 'St. Thomas', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'st-thomas', 'desc_html': 'Cruises that visit St. Thomas offer some of the best photo opportunities in the Caribbean. That&rsquo;s why a Carnival cruise to the Virgin Islands tops many folk&rsquo;s vacation wish lists. Seafarers from around the globe have flocked to the sheltered harbors of St. Thomas since pirates sailed these seas. Today, cruises to St. Thomas dock in one of the busiest and most developed ports in the West Indies: Charlotte Amalie, the island&rsquo;s historic capital. Immerse yourself in the rhythm of the market bustle, and swing to the beat of scratch bands. Or plant yourself on a beautiful beach and relax the day away. The choice is yours when you cruise to St. Thomas in the U.S. Virgin Islands.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Play on the creamy white sands of Magens Bay Beach.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Get up close to sea horses and tropical fish at Coral World.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Charter a sailboat to explore secret coves and turquoise bays.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Toast your cruise to St. Thomas at a beach bar in Frenchtown.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-st-thomas-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'STX', 'name': 'St. Croix', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'st-croix', 'desc_html': 'Cruises to St Croix offer some of the most striking scenery you can see on a cruise &mdash; on land, on the water, and beneath it. The island also has a fascinating history. St. Croix&rsquo;s path to becoming a U.S. Virgin Island took it through the hands of France and Denmark. While we&rsquo;re talking geography, cruises to St. Croix let you explore a variety of it, ranging from the east end&rsquo;s desert vistas to rainforest and palm trees on the west. Underwater, coral reefs are abundant, making SCUBA diving a great way to see best-hidden local sights during cruises to St Croix. As far as unwinding goes, there&rsquo;s rum &mdash; the good stuff &mdash; and plenty of it, with famous brands&rsquo; distilleries located right here.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore 40,000 acres of land and sea across Buck Island Reef National Monument.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See St. George Botanical Garden, with plants from cacti to exotic lush rainforest flora.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Get the full tour of the Cruzan Rum Distillery to see &mdash; and sample &mdash; the distillation process.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tour the nearby Christiansted, learn about local Danish history and explore Fort Christiansvaern.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-st-croix-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SVN', 'name': 'Savona', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'savona', 'desc_html': "Might Savona be overshadowed by its more famous nearby neighbors? Maybe sometimes, but the hidden charm of this Italian Riviera town makes it a stop you shouldn't miss while cruising the region.\xa0Savona was long protected by the 16th-century Primar Fortezza (good guess — that's a fortress!), which still seems to keep a watchful eye on the waters of the Gulf of Genoa, while welcoming visitors inside to stroll among its high walls, tunnels and even a museum. But don't miss walking the medieval streets of Via Pia and Via Paleocapa, not to mention stopping in to some of Savona's selection of cathedrals, including its own Sistine Chapel. While this one is certainly smaller than the iconic\xa0Vatican chapel, it features incredibly ornate walls and domed ceiling that make it a great example of the style.", 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-savona-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SVQ', 'name': 'Cádiz (Seville)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'cadiz-seville', 'desc_html': 'Cádiz dates back to 1100 B.C., making it actually one of the oldest cities not just in the region of Andalusia, not just in Spain, but in all of Europe! The city’s strategic location at the mouth of the Mediterranean may explain its architectural landscape — which features over 100 watchtowers — and a clue to why it’s home to Spain’s navy. Further inland in the region is the city of Seville, which boasts a past not quite as long, but definitely rich with history! Highlights in Seville include the 1,100-year-old royal palace of Alcazar replete with gardens and fountains, an opulent 15th-century cathedral — actually, Europe’s third largest — and even the hillside village Arcos de la Frontera, whose city center was officially declared a national artistic-historic monument.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-seville-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SXM', 'name': 'St. Maarten', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'st-maarten', 'desc_html': '<p>Explore two colorful nations on one exotic island on one vacation. Split down the middle centuries ago by two European powers, this 37-mile isle offers cosmopolitan culture, international shopping, and world-class cuisine with a laid-back Caribbean atmosphere. Cruise to St. Maarten and you&rsquo;ll find the island&rsquo;s natural attributes are equally fine: the rugged coastline shelters silky crescents of sand framed by green undulating hills. Enjoy the laidback vibe of the beach or put on your hiking shoes and explore ruins of historic forts. One thing&rsquo;s for sure &mdash; when you cruise to St. Maarten you&rsquo;ll come home with amazing memories that will last a lifetime.</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Experience the thrill of racing the famous 12-meter race boats.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Shop the duty-free stores along the Philipsburg waterfront.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Swing to calypso sounds at a barefoot beach bar.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Hike through the ruins of French and Dutch forts overlooking the sparkling Caribbean Sea.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-st-maarten-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'SYN', 'name': 'Sydney, NS', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'sydney', 'desc_html': 'Australia’s famous city isn’t the only Sydney worth cruising to! While exploring Canada & New England on a Carnival cruise, you can dig deeper into a pocket of Canadian history, a city that was actually founded in the late 18th century by loyalist British soldiers retreating from the American Revolution. Robust industries fueled by the region’s natural resources sprang up, leading to the place you’ll enjoy exploring today. Start at the harbor — you can’t miss it because of the huge fiddle! It’s the world’s largest and hints at the live music (sea shanties, anyone?) you might experience while dining at the waterfront restaurants enjoying freshly-caught seafood. There’s actual history to explore here, with the entire Fortress of Louisbourg having been painstakingly recreated from its original rubble to showcase a pivotal location from the Seven Years’ War. Alexander Graham Bell’s house is another shouldn’t-miss for fans of the inventive spirit that spurred modern communications as we know it.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-canada-itinerary-sydney-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'TFJ', 'name': 'Cruise Tracy Arm Fjord', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'cruise-tracy-arm-fjord', 'desc_html': 'One of the most spectacular cruise destinations on earth, Tracy Arm Fjord is actually made up of two separate fjords. Each fjord is over 30 miles long, and a full fifth of their area is covered in ice… not to mention the glaciers, truly one of nature’s most dramatic and breathtaking sights. With these huge chunks of sliding ice, hundreds of waterfalls and a variety of native wildlife, you won’t even want to blink as you cruise through this natural wonder.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-alaska-itinerary-tracy-arm-fjord-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'TLL', 'name': 'Tallinn', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'tallinn', 'desc_html': 'Contemporary chic meets medieval charm in Tallinn, Estonia, located on the Baltic Sea. When you take a Carnival cruise to Tallinn, you’ll discover a vibrant capital city full of rich culture, hidden history, and picture-perfect streets. The city has preserved its limestone city walls that encircle the Old Town and 14th-century churches. As you wander through the town, you’ll see why Tallinn is a UNESCO World Heritage Site. While here, you can experience the city’s Gothic Town Hall Square, see the war monument at Freedom Square and visit the Rotermann Quarter.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take a stroll along the famous cobbled walkway St. Catherine’s Passage.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Admire stunning views of Old Town from St. Olaf’s Church tower.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Step back in time to Tallinn’s 20th-century history in the Vabamu Museum of Occupations and Freedom.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the grand Alexander Nevsky Cathedral atop Toompea Hill.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-tallinn-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'TNG', 'name': 'Tangier', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'tangier', 'desc_html': " You can find Tangier right at\xa0the Strait of Gibraltar, the narrow passageway that serves as the stunning front door to the Mediterranean Sea. When writing your own Tangier story, you're likely to focus on\xa0the iconic Medina, and this old-city neighborhood is packed with things to see scattered around narrow, winding streets that trade modernity for old-time charm. Traversing it rewards visitors handsomely, with top sights like the Kasbah, the former home of the Sultan of Morocco,\xa0lively street shopping experiences,\xa0a lookout viewpoint, and even a museum dedicated to Tangier's long relationship with the United States. You can even go beyond the Medina and check out the Grand Socco square, explore regional attractions like Tétouan or simply stroll the the Mediterranean's edge.", 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-tangier-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'TOR', 'name': 'Tortola', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'tortola', 'desc_html': 'If you&rsquo;re looking for some of the most scenic blue ocean vistas in the Caribbean, you&rsquo;ll find them on cruises to the British Virgin Islands. How many other islands give you the chance to sail on channel-crossing yachts destined for the Norman, Cooper, Salt or Pepper Islands? On cruises to Tortola, you can reach all of these, or jump right in and swim or snorkel into underwater caves and get up-close with colorful coral reefs. Another highlight of cruises to the British Virgin Islands is a scenic island tour that takes you up Fort Hill to Cane Garden Bay, where you can relax on spectacular white-sand beaches. Enjoy the tales of this historic waterway as you retrace the paths of Christopher Columbus and Sir Francis Drake on Carnival&rsquo;s cruises to Tortola.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Experience the world famous Baths at Virgin Gorda.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>The tallest mountain in all the Virgin Islands can be found in Sage Mountain Park.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Nearby Salt Island was once in habited by residents who sent Queen Elizabeth a one-pound bag per year as rent.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-tortola-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'TPA', 'name': 'Tampa', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'tampa', 'desc_html': 'Set sail from Florida&rsquo;s Gulf Coast and you&rsquo;ll discover just how convenient &mdash; and action-packed &mdash; cruises out of Tampa can be. Welcome to one of Florida&rsquo;s busiest ports &mdash; where the historically Cuban district of Ybor City, the aquarium, city shopping and local art museums are all in easy reach. Wide beaches and urban adventures are also at your fingertips when you book a Carnival cruise from Tampa. And come nightfall, 7th Avenue in Ybor City heats up, Latin-style.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Step into a surreal universe at St. Petersburg&rsquo;s Salvador Dal&iacute; Museum.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Collect shells by sunset on the beaches of St. Pete and Clearwater.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Canoe or kayak down the meandering Hillsborough River.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-tampa-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'TYO', 'name': 'Tokyo', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'tokyo', 'desc_html': 'Like so many important port towns, Edo started off as a sleepy fishing village. This one, however, surprisingly grew up to become Japan’s capital, the biggest metro area on earth… and was later renamed “Tokyo.” For decades now it’s felt a bit like it’s living in the future… and you can probably say it is, with all the tech and neon and energy that flows throughout iconic neighborhoods like Akihabra and Shibuya. But with all the upgrades installed, Tokyo’s traditional culture hasn’t been replaced, best seen through the residential neighborhoods of narrow streets lined with traditional homes. And that’s not to mention the green spaces, like the city’s ample national parks, gardens, shrines and temples. Some can’t-miss spots are Imperial Palace Plaza in the city center, Tokyo Tower — which tops even the Eiffel Tower — plus the imposing Mount Fuji is always happy to join the city’s skyline for a photo.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-transpacific-itinerary-tokyo-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'VGO', 'name': 'Vigo', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'vigo', 'desc_html': 'Vigo was founded around local fishing roots, and time has proven this to be a good call &mdash; today the city boasts one of the largest seaports in Spain. This is where you come in: a cruise to Vigo is definitely the right way to visit this city! Enjoy a walk through El Castro, the 17th century fortress overlooking the port &mdash; stroll through gardens as lovely as the sea views. From Vigo, you can explore Santiago de Compostela, the capital city of the Spain&rsquo;s Galicia region, whose &ldquo;Old Town&rdquo; neighborhood was declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1985.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the St. James Cathedral, built on the location where his remains were said to be discovered.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Taste some of the finest wines in Galicia\'s Albari&ntilde;o wine country.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-port-vigo-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'VLT', 'name': 'Malta', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'valletta', 'desc_html': 'Malta&rsquo;s the big sister, the largest island in a seven-strong archipelago just a stone&rsquo;s throw from Europe&hellip; and not far at all from Africa. The island&rsquo;s history began with the megalithic stone temples at Gozo, which may just be the oldest free-standing structures on Earth. Valletta is Malta&rsquo;s capital, and its bustling streets are lined with superb Baroque buildings, palaces, gardens and churches. The city has been declared a World Heritage Site by UNESCO and its nickname is Superbissima (&ldquo;most proud&rdquo;). Malta has two official languages: Maltese, the national language, and English. Malta was admitted to the European Union in 2004, and four years later became part of the Eurozone.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll the Old Cathedral and Ramparts of the so-called Silent City.</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>See the Palazzo Parisio, a 19th century palace whose gardens have earned it the nickname “the miniature Versailles.”</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stop in to Casa Rocca Piccola, whose 50 rooms housed Maltese nobility for over 400 years.</li>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-malta-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'WAR', 'name': 'Warnemünde (Berlin)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'warnemunde-berlin', 'desc_html': 'Old meets new on your Berlin cruise. Here you will see how this once turbulent city is now a bustling cosmopolitan cultural mecca. In the capital and largest city in Germany, you certainly won’t run out of things to do. The Berlin Wall isn’t the same as it used to be, so take a trip to see the remains of this historic wall. You can also discover Egyptian mummies on Museum Island or step inside the historic parliament building known as the Reichstag.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Learn about the city’s former East-West divide at Checkpoint Charlie.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Marvel at a reconstructed neo-Assyrian palace and an ancient Babylonian gate at the Pergamonmuseum.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the huge glass dome in the Reichstag parliament building.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Munch on a local favorite, currywurst, a snack offered at buzzing food stands.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-itinerary-berlin-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'WRF', 'name': 'Bermuda', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'bermuda', 'desc_html': 'Kick back amidst the sun-kissed pleasures of a pink-sand paradise on Carnival cruises to King&rsquo;s Wharf. This British overseas territory of Bermuda has a rich naval heritage&hellip; plus powdery beaches fringed in coconut palms. Located at the very tip of Bermuda&rsquo;s glittering archipelago of over 100 islets and cays, King&rsquo;s Wharf was made for lounging in the Gulf Stream&rsquo;s balmy subtropical clime, which meanders between Bermuda and mainland North America.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Explore underwater shipwrecks in the turquoise seas.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Dig your feet into the soft pink sand on one of Bermuda&rsquo;s 34 beautiful beaches.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Tee up on world-class golf courses on a King&rsquo;s Wharf, Bermuda cruise.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Join the Bermudans for a proper British afternoon tea.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-caribbean-itinerary-bermuda-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'WSY', 'name': 'Airlie Beach', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'airlie-beach', 'desc_html': 'The white sands of world-famous Whitehaven Beach, glass-bottom-boat day tours on the turquoise waters of the Coral Sea, high-speed catamaran joy rides and Hamilton Island region magic await on a cruise to the Whitsundays with Carnival. Travel to the heart of the 74 islands that make up the picture-perfect Whitsunday Islands, one of Australia\'s most stunning destinations, where you can snorkel the Great Barrier Reef, swim in crystal-clear waters and lose yourself in ancient tropical rainforests. Sail on a 4, 7, 9, or 10-day cruise departing Sydney or Brisbane, and enjoy more than 45 onboard activities for the whole family from the moment you step aboard.<br /><br />\n\nCruises from Airlie Beach to the Whitsundays offer the kind of port days that suit everyone, whether you\'re after flat-out adventure on the water, a scenic flight above it, or simply a coffee and a wonder at the beautiful scenery. For a deeper look at everything the region has to offer, the Whitsundays cruises guide is worth a read before you go. Here\'s what a port day in the Whitsundays can look like. <br /><br />\n\nFew port days start with quite this much adrenaline. The Ocean Rafting tour sends you hurtling through the Whitsunday Passage at speed, then drops anchor off Hook or Black Island so you can snorkel straight off the raft into living coral, with an eco-guide on hand to tell you exactly what you\'re swimming through.<br /><br />\n\nThere\'s something about the sound of sails filling with wind that makes everything slow down in the best possible way. Scenic Sailing puts you on a classic Australian yacht for a long, unhurried reach across to Langford Island, with breakfast, lunch and as much Great Barrier Reef snorkelling as you can fit into a single afternoon. <br /><br />\n\nNothing puts Whitehaven Beach in perspective quite like seeing it from the air. The Reef and Island Scenic Flight sweep low over the swirling silica sands of Hill Inlet, traces the outline of Heart Reef from above, and reminds you, with some force, just how extraordinary this corner of Queensland actually is. <br /><br />\n\nWhen the heat settles in mid-afternoon, the Airlie Beach Lagoon is a great place to be. Stinger-safe, beautifully landscaped and completely free, it\'s the kind of place you find a patch of shade, slip into the water and quietly decide you could stay here indefinitely.<p>If you’re looking for an inland experience, a variety of activities are available, such as:</p>\n    <ul class="features-list">\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Full day or half day scenic must-see Queensland tours. \n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Take a day trip to the Conway National Park or walk around Shute Harbour.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n       Enjoy boutique shopping at the Port of Airlie.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Take a boat ride and cruise Whitsunday Islands, coves, and coral reefs.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        <em class="dest-check"></em>\n        Experience a jet boat or jet ski, or go ocean rafting.\n    </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/AU/Australia-AirlieBeach-Tropical-Island-Aerial-Shoreline-v1-1920x1080-jpg.jpg'},
    {'code': 'YHZ', 'name': 'Halifax, NS', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'halifax', 'desc_html': 'Your first look at Halifax, Nova Scotia is from across the enormous natural harbor that also hosts the verdant George&rsquo;s Island. Ships have arrived at this key Atlantic seaport just like this for centuries, including both the million immigrants who passed through in the 1900s, as well as the Halifax salvage boats recovering wreckage from the Titanic. Besides a modern city abuzz with museums and shops, you&rsquo;ll find a massive fort overlooking the waterfront and idyllic villages for postcard-perfect nature walks on your Halifax cruise.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Meet a Scottish regiment at the Halifax Citadel National Historic Site.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Laze under the gazebo at the Public Gardens on Halifax cruises.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take in the views from the Peggy&rsquo;s Cove lighthouse.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Hear heartbreaking stories of immigrants and war brides at Pier 21.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-canada-itinerary-halifax-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'YPR', 'name': 'Prince Rupert, BC', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'prince-rupert', 'desc_html': 'You can probably tell that Prince Rupert, British Columbia is a little more laid back, less bustling than other places, thanks to its nickname: “The City of Rainbows.” It may have more to do with the climate, but the name still fits, with welcoming, photo-worthy natural sights that even the frequently moist weather can’t dampen. It’s easy to be this beautiful with a cast of local wildlife like Prince Rupert has, with grizzly bears, humpback whales and eagles making up just a few of the stars. The local museums are another spot to get a feel for the area, whether it’s art, culture or, say, railroads you’re into. And definitely stop into the local shops, plus restaurants that are proud to serve up fresh-caught local delicacies.', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-canada-itinerary-prince-rupert-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'YSJ', 'name': 'Saint John, NB', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'saint-john', 'desc_html': '<p>Cruises to Canada offer some of the most dramatic scenes Mother Nature has to offer. Sail with Carnival for some of the best views of the Canadian coastline on a cruise to Saint John. Nestled between nature parks and the powerful currents of the Bay of Fundy, Saint John is the province of New Brunswick&rsquo;s largest city and its most important port. Set out from your Carnival cruise into Downtown, with its Victorian-era architecture and bustling central market. Your ship anchors in the Bay of Fundy, where you&rsquo;ll spot seals and shorebirds from the trail, your kayak, or from an observation tower. Whether you take to the trails for a hike or just take some time off in town, your cruise to Saint John is bound to be one you won&rsquo;t soon forget.</p><ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Watch the swirling tide crash one way &mdash; and within the hour turn completely around &mdash; at the unique Reversing Falls.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Hike past misshapen rocks and over gorges on the Fundy Trail Parkway.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Snag some local baked goods at the Saint John City Market.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Make friends with the wildlife at Irving Nature Park.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-canada-itinerary-st-john-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'YYJ', 'name': 'Victoria', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'victoria', 'desc_html': 'Carnival cruises to Victoria, British Columbia call on this genteel provincial capital, which you&rsquo;ll find perched on the southern tip of Vancouver Island. Packed with reminders of its rich British heritage, Victoria is fronted by water, filled with gardens, and backed by mountains. All the finest sights on Victoria cruises are clustered around the Inner Harbour, from a world-class museum to scenic waterfront parks&hellip; plus a deliciously decadent setting for afternoon tea.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>See what&rsquo;s in bloom at Butchart Gardens during your cruise to Victoria, British Columbia.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll the trim grounds of the Parliament Buildings.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Investigate the elaborate masks of the native &ldquo;First Nations&rdquo; peoples at the Royal BC Museum.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Wend your way around Inner Harbor past Victoria&rsquo;s most iconic sights.\n    </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-alaska-itinerary-victoria-bc-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'YYT', 'name': "St. John's, NL", 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'st-john-s', 'desc_html': '', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-canada-itinerary-st-johns-newfoundland-3.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ZEE', 'name': 'Zeebrugge (Brussels)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'zeebrugge-brussels', 'desc_html': 'Zeebrugge offers plenty of adventure choices for your Belgium visit. Nearby Brussels is a great option, with two very different areas rolled into one city that offers something for everyone. Old Brussels is a historic region that celebrates the ancient – amazing architecture, a Royal District, and majestic cathedrals that are rich in both history and beauty. New Brussels is a bit trendier locality that houses many vital institutions in the European Quarter, including the European Commission and the European Parliament. Add to your adventure at the nearby medieval town of Bruges. Visit the Rozenhoedkaai canal and enjoy the most scenic views in the city, then take in the towering Belfry, standing 270-feet tall in the city centre and part a UNESCO world heritage site.<ul class="features-list">\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Discover the ancient Guild Halls in Bruges, and the Basilica of the Holy Blood.</li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Ride along the picturesque canals of Bruges, a great way to experience all the sites this medieval city has to offer. </li>\n<li><em class="dest-check"></em>Visit the impressive St. Bavo&rsquo;s Cathedral in the medieval city of Ghent, also home of the well-known artwork &ldquo;The Adoration of the Mystic Lamb.&rdquo;</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-europe-port-zeebrugge-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'ZJO', 'name': 'Zihuatanejo (Ixtapa)', 'is_homeport': False, 'slug': 'zihuatanejo-ixtapa', 'desc_html': 'Divide your day between million-dollar resorts and a sleepy fishing village on your Carnival cruise to Ixtapa, Mexico. These Pacific Coast sister towns couldn\'t be any more different: younger Ixtapa is all flashy high-rises and manicured golf courses, while neighbor Zihuatanejo is a working fishing village. Cruise to Ixtapa, Mexico to experience the lush life on Ixtapa\'s Playa Palmar and nurse a 20-peso beer at Zihuatanejo\'s laid-back Playa Las Gatas.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Pose with the glitzy hotels on Playa Palmar when you cruise to Ixtapa, Mexico.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Gallop through the waves on horseback at Playa Linda.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Watch the tide roll in from your seaside table at Playa La Ropa.&nbsp;</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Wade in the calm shallows at Playa Las Gatas.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-mexico-itinerary-zihuatanejo-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LAX', 'name': 'Long Beach (Los Angeles)', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'long-beach-los-angeles', 'desc_html': 'When we talk about cruising from Los Angeles, fyi: we&rsquo;re talking about cruises from Long Beach. A short drive from LA is where you&rsquo;ll find this seaside Southern California city that&rsquo;s inseparable from its big-city neighbor, while undeniably moving to its own local beat. Dotted with dozens of parks, beaches and multiple public golf courses (fore times five!), Long Beach also boasts perhaps the world&rsquo;s most unique hotel &mdash; located aboard the old-time ocean liner The Queen Mary (which is haunted, or so go the rumors). You can experience it before one of Carnival&rsquo;s cruises from Long Beach, but definitely don&rsquo;t miss the glitzy, big-city Los Angeles &mdash; the right place to experience the left-coast life. Take in the storied sights of this City of Angels, from its modern museums and high-end shopping to its funky seaside towns and star-studded SoCal sights dotting the hills and boulevards. Hollywood &mdash; hooray! So if you&rsquo;re dreaming about a cruise from Los Angeles, remember: Carnival&rsquo;s cruises from Long Beach are just the ticket.<ul class="features-list">\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Climb aboard the <em>Queen Mary</em>, a glamorous 1930s ocean liner.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Find your favorite star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Stroll through the art and antiquities of the Getty Center<sup style="font-size: 70%;">&reg;</sup>.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Take the backlot tour of Universal Studios<sup style="font-size: 70%;">&trade;</sup> for a look at Hollywood mythmaking.</li>\n    <li><em class="dest-check"></em>Gaze into the starry night sky through the Griffith Observatory\'s<sup style="font-size: 70%;">&reg;</sup> giant telescope.</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itineraries-los-angeles-1.jpg'},
    {'code': 'LON', 'name': 'Dover (London)', 'is_homeport': True, 'slug': 'dover-london', 'desc_html': 'Be captivated by cliff-top walks and 2,000 years of history on cruises from Dover, England. Set against the backdrop of the White Cliffs and peering across to France on the other side of the English Channel, Dover&rsquo;s setting is a sight to behold. This bustling English port is steeped in history and coastal beauty. Explore the secret tunnels beneath medieval Dover Castle and easily make your way to iconic London landmarks like Buckingham Palace and the House of Parliament.<ul class="features-list">\n\t<li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tFollow in King Henry II&rsquo;s footsteps at Dover Castle.\n\t</li>\n    <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tFeel the power of the sea as you hike along the White Cliffs of Dover.\n\t</li>\n    <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tImmerse yourself in the City of Canterbury, literary setting of Chaucer&rsquo;s epic tales.\n\t</li>\n    <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tCatch the changing of the guard at Buckingham Palace.\n\t</li>\n  <li>\n\t\t<em class="dest-check"></em>\n\t\tSnap a selfie in front of Big Ben, London&rsquo;s celebrity clock tower.\n\t</li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/-/media/Images/explore/destinations/ports/carnival-home-port-itinerary-london-dover-1.jpg'},
]